/* 段落记忆 · 词层 2 · 子块 c：词头 → {tw:[关系词,关系类型], en, zh} */
window.APP_MERGE_NET(2,{"sub":"c","par":{"lend":{"tw":[["trust",3],["borrow",1],["invest",6],["advance",3],["add",0],["bring",0],["change",2],["contribute",0]],"en":"My uncle works in a small bank. He will lend money only to people he can trust. Before he signs anything, he asks what the borrower plans to do with it. Some customers want to borrow a large amount and invest it in a new shop; others need a small advance to buy a machine. He says a good loan must add something to the town, not only bring profit to one family. When a business fails, he will change the plan instead of taking the house. That is why so many people contribute to his fund and wait for months.","zh":"我舅舅在一家小银行工作。他只把钱借给他信得过的人。签字之前，他一定会问借款人打算拿去做什么。有些客户想借一大笔投进新开的店，另一些人只差一笔小预支来买台机器。他说，一笔好贷款应该给镇上添点什么，而不只是给一户人家带来利润。生意做垮了，他会改方案，而不是收房子。所以那么多人都愿意往他的资金里凑份子，还愿意等上几个月。"},"refuse":{"tw":[["deny",0],["resist",0],["decline",0],["accept",1],["agree",6],["bounce",3],["regret",3],["waste",2]],"en":"My father had to refuse a job in another city. He did not want to deny the offer, but the family could not move. For a week he tried to resist the good salary, and at last he had to decline politely. The manager would not accept his first answer and called again; my father stayed calm and did not agree to change his mind. The letter the firm sent came back with a bounce and a short note. He says he does not regret the choice, though he still feels he wasted the chance of an easier life.","zh":"父亲不得不拒绝另一座城市的一份工作。他并不想否认这个邀约，但一家人搬不过去。他硬撑了一个星期没被那份高薪说动，最后还是客气地辞谢了。经理不肯接受他第一次的回答，又打来电话；父亲很平静，也没答应改主意。公司寄出的信被退了回来，上面附了一张便条。他说自己不后悔这个选择，只是仍觉得浪费了一个过得更轻松的机会。"},"receive":{"tw":[["receiver",4],["find",0],["hear",3],["reception",4],["accept",2],["pay",6],["recipient",4],["see",3]],"en":"The old radio stopped working last summer. My grandfather had to receive the morning news from a small receiver that he built himself. He would find the right station by turning a metal wheel, and often he could not hear the words well. He could still see the faces of the singers in his mind. One day a parcel arrived for him: a new radio, sent by a former student. The reception that evening was perfect, and the first song made him laugh. He was happy to accept the gift, though he refused to pay for the delivery. The recipient of that kindness still writes a letter every year.","zh":"去年夏天那台旧收音机不响了。爷爷只能靠一台自己装的小接收机收听早间新闻。他转动一个金属旋钮找电台，常常听不清词句。可他还是能在脑子里看见歌手们的脸。有一天他收到一个包裹：一台新收音机，是一位从前的学生寄来的。那天晚上的信号好极了，第一首歌就把他逗笑了。他很高兴收下这份礼物，却不肯付运费。这份心意的受赠者，如今每年都还会写一封信来。"},"repeat":{"tw":[["repetitive",4],["echo",0],["quote",3],["play",2],["recur",0],["cycle",3],["act",2]],"en":"The teacher asked us to repeat the last line of the poem. Nobody wanted to do it, because the words were repetitive and long. My friend read it twice, and the echo of her voice filled the hall. She likes to quote old writers, so she added a line from a play. Then someone asked whether the same question would recur in the exam. The teacher said the cycle of every lesson was the same: listen, repeat, act, and then write. I wrote the whole line on my page and read it to my little brother. He took the part of the hero and we both laughed.","zh":"老师让我们重复这首诗的最后一句。没人愿意，因为那些词又长又重复。我朋友读了两遍，她的声音在大厅里回荡。她喜欢引用老作家的句子，于是又加了一句戏里的台词。有人接着问，同样的问题考试里会不会再出现。老师说，每节课的循环都一样：听、重复、动手演、然后写。我把整句抄在本子上，读给我弟弟听。他演了里面那个英雄，我们俩都笑了。"},"produce":{"tw":[["farm",0],["grow",0],["raise",0],["carry",3],["cut",3],["change",2],["generate",6],["product",4]],"en":"On a small farm near the coast, two families produce olive oil. They grow the trees on dry land and raise a few goats between the rows. Every autumn they carry the fruit to the old press in the village. Workers cut the branches by hand and gather them into tall piles, and the whole change takes three weeks. A new machine would generate heat and take less time, but the oil might lose its taste. The product is now sold in shops far away, and the label shows the name of the village.","zh":"海边的一个小农场上，两家人一起榨橄榄油。他们在旱地上种树，还在树行间养了几只山羊。每年秋天，他们把果子运到村里的老压榨坊。工人用手修剪枝条、堆成高高的垛，整个轮换要三周。新机器发热、省时间，但油可能就没有那个味道了。如今这产品卖到了很远的商店里，标签上印着村子的名字。"},"recall":{"tw":[["remember",0],["return",0],["concentrate",2],["mind",3],["think",0],["recognize",3],["announce",6],["issue",1]],"en":"When my grandmother began to recall the war years, she could remember the smallest details. She could return to a street in her old town and describe each shop door. I had to concentrate hard to follow her, because her mind moved from one year to another. Sometimes she would stop and think for a long time before she went on. She could recognize a name on a list that the museum would announce that month. The issue of memory, she said, is not what you lose but what you choose to keep.","zh":"奶奶开始回忆战争那些年时，最小的细节她都记得。她能回到老家的一条街上，把每个店门都描述出来。我得使劲集中精神才跟得上，因为她的思绪会在不同年份之间来回跳。有时她会停下来想很久，再往下说。名单上的名字，博物馆那个月要公布谁，她都能认出来。她说，记忆这件事，问题不在你丢掉了什么，而在于你选择留下什么。"},"lean":{"tw":[["leaner",4],["list",3],["weather",3],["move",2],["rich",1],["soft",6],["run",0],["suffer",3],["position",2],["medium",6],["tend",0]],"en":"At the market my father would lean over the counter and ask for the leaner cut of meat. He kept a short list of the sellers he trusted. He said the weather that year had been hard on the cattle, and the poorer farms would suffer. A rich man in a soft coat stood beside us and chose a medium piece without a word. My father did not move from his position. He would tend to his own business. Then he ran his hand over the meat and said it was good enough to cook slowly. We walked home in the cold.","zh":"在市场上，我爸总会伏在柜台上，要那块瘦一些的肉。他有一张短短的名单，记着他信得过的卖主。他说那年天气对牛不好，穷些的农场要吃不消了。一个穿软呢大衣的有钱人站在我们旁边，一句话不说就挑了块中等的。我爸一动不动，守着自己的位置。他自己的事他自己管。然后他用手在肉上抹了一下，说这块炖着吃够好了。天冷，我们走回了家。"},"qualify":{"tw":[["quality",4],["condition",0],["provide",3],["add",2],["disqualify",1],["eligible",6],["dispose",0],["stamp",3],["prepare",2],["win",6],["modify",0]],"en":"My cousin trained all spring to qualify for the running team, and her condition was the best it had ever been. The coach would provide new shoes if she could win the school race. She had to add two more laps each week and prepare for the heat. One small mistake could disqualify her, so she checked her form like a stamp on a letter. The judges said she was eligible, though the rules might change and modify the distance. She kept her old shoes, and would not dispose of the worn pair. On the day she came third, and the quality of her run pleased everyone.","zh":"我表妹练了一整个春天，想拿到跑步队的资格，她的状态从没这么好过。教练说，只要她能赢下校赛，就给配新鞋。她每周得多跑两圈，还得为高温做准备。一个小失误就可能让她被取消资格，所以她像检查信封上的邮票那样检查自己的姿势。裁判说她是合格的，不过规矩也许会改，距离也可能调整。她把那双旧鞋留着，舍不得扔掉这双穿旧了的。比赛那天她拿了第三，她跑步的样子让所有人都满意。"},"repair":{"tw":[["reparation",4],["doctor",0],["care",3],["better",2],["break",1],["damage",6],["fix",0],["fill",3],["pay",2],["upgrade",6],["amend",0]],"en":"The roof of the old shed needed a repair before the rain came. My uncle asked the doctor who lived next door to take a look, though it was not really his care. The wind had done some damage in March, and a loose board could break at any moment. He had to fix it himself and fill the gap with new wood. He would pay for the better tiles and hoped to upgrade the whole roof later. He said he might amend the plan, but he would want no reparation from anyone. It took two quiet afternoons, and the shed was dry again.","zh":"老棚子的屋顶趁雨还没来得修一修。我叔请隔壁住的那位医生来看看，虽然这事本不归他管。三月的风弄坏了一些地方，一块松了的木板随时可能断掉。他只好自己动手，用新木料把缝填上。他愿意花钱买好一点的瓦，还打算以后再整修整个屋顶。他说计划也许会改一改，可他不指望谁来赔。两个安静的下午下来，棚子又不漏了。"},"object":{"tw":[["objectify",4],["aim",0],["catch",3],["goal",2],["visible",6],["objective",0],["head",3],["content",2],["particular",6],["target",0]],"en":"At the airport a guard asked me to place every sharp object on the tray, and he pointed to a particular bag with a long tube inside. His aim was simple: to catch anything that could do harm. The security officer had one clear objective, and he would not let it out of sight until the bag was visible on the screen. I turned my head away while a second guard checked the contents. He said they did not want to objectify people, only to reach a goal. On the wall above him hung a target with a red circle, just for practice.","zh":"在机场，一名安检员让我把所有尖锐物品放到托盘上，还指着一只里面装着长管子的包。他的目的很简单：把任何可能伤人的东西截下来。这位安检员有一个明确的目标，在包出现在屏幕上之前，他的目光一直不离开它。我扭过头去，另一个安检员在查看里面的东西。他说他们不是要把人当成物件，只是想达成一个目的。他上方的墙上挂着一个带红圈的靶子，纯粹用来练手。"},"observe":{"tw":[["observance",4],["discover",0],["bird",3],["accept",2],["participate",6],["find",0],["see",3],["check",2],["conclude",6],["follow",0]],"en":"Every April my uncle would observe the birds that came back to the marsh, and he never missed the old observance of counting them. He would follow the same path, check every nest, and write down what he could see. Last year he managed to discover a new pair near the water. He asked me to participate in the count, but I was too slow. I had to accept that he knew the marsh better than I did. From the numbers we could conclude that the colony was growing, and he would find some small comfort in that. It was a good morning.","zh":"每年四月，我叔都会去观察回到这片沼泽的鸟，他从不错过数鸟这桩老规矩。他会沿着同一条路走，逐个查看鸟巢，把看到的记下来。去年他在水边发现了一对新来的鸟。他让我一起参加这次清点，可我动作太慢。我只得承认他对这片沼泽比我熟。从数目上我们能断定鸟群在增多，他也从中得着一点小小的安慰。那是个挺好的早晨。"},"oppose":{"tw":[["opponent",4],["fight",0],["buck",3],["act",2],["reject",6],["match",0],["protest",3],["argue",2],["objected",6],["react",0]],"en":"Many people in the town began to oppose the plan to build a new road through the park. They said they would fight it and protest in front of the hall. One man said he would buck the whole scheme on his own. His opponent in the debate was a young officer who refused to act in a hurry. The two began to argue, and each tried to reject the other's numbers. A teacher who had objected to the plan last year joined them. The crowd waited to see how the officer would react. In the end the match of words changed nothing that day.","zh":"镇上许多人开始反对穿过公园修一条新路的计划。他们说会抗争，还会在市政厅前抗议。有个人说他要单枪匹马把整个计划顶回去。辩论中他的对手是一位年轻的官员，那人说什么也不肯急着行动。两人争了起来，各自都想把对方的数据驳回去。一位去年就反对过这计划的老师也加入了。人群等着看那位官员怎么反应。到头来，那场口舌之争那天什么也没改变。"},"patch":{"tw":[["patchy",4],["piece",0],["bed",3],["join",2],["skin",6],["garden",3],["repair",2],["thick",6],["spot",0],["spell",0]],"en":"In the garden behind the house, one patch of grass had gone patchy and brown. My mother cut a thick piece of turf from the far corner and pressed it into the bare spot. She had to join the edges with her hands and hold them for a long while. That bed of flowers had been her project, and she would not let it die. As she worked, a spell of hot weather passed and the small repair began to take. She said the ground under her skin had a memory of rain, and it would come back. Then she washed her hands and sat down.","zh":"屋后的园子里，有一块草地变得斑斑驳驳、发黄了。我妈从远角切下一块厚厚的草皮，按到那块光秃的地方。她得用手把边缝对严，再按住好一阵子。那片花坛一直是她的宝贝，她不肯让它就这么枯掉。她干着活，一段热天过去了，这处小小的修补开始生效。她说地底下贴着草皮的那层还记着雨，雨总会回来的。然后她洗了手，坐了下来。"},"pipe":{"tw":[["piper",4],["tube",0],["main",3],["play",2],["metal",6],["shriek",0],["drain",3],["shout",2],["shaft",6],["shrill",0]],"en":"One winter morning a water pipe burst in the clinic, and a thin tube of metal began to shriek. The main had frozen overnight, and water ran down the drain in the wall. A worker shouted for help, and the sound was so shrill that it hurt. Somewhere upstairs a child was learning to play a tune on a small pipe, and a piper in the street answered, as if in a game. We had to open a long shaft in the floor to find the leak. Nobody could shout above the noise until the water was shut off. It was a strange morning at the clinic.","zh":"一个冬天的早上，诊所里一根水管爆了，一截细细的金属管尖叫起来。主管道夜里冻住了，水顺着墙里的排水沟往下淌。一个工人喊人来帮忙，那声音尖得刺耳。楼上有户人家的孩子正学着在短短的笛子上吹一支曲子，街上一个吹笛的人应和着，像在做游戏。我们只得在地板上开一道长槽去找漏水的地方。水没关掉之前，谁的声音都压不过那动静。诊所里这个早上怪得很。"},"pole":{"tw":[["polar",4],["rod",0],["boom",3],["end",2],["lap",6],["terminal",0],["mast",3],["hold",2],["race",6],["perch",0]],"en":"On the day of the boat race, a tall mast stood beside the pole at the end of the pier. A man with a long rod raised a flag, and the boom swung over the water. The wind was cold, like a polar current off the ice. My cousin had to hold the rope tight during the first lap and watch the terminal light on the shore. A bird came to perch on the top of the pole and would not move. The crowd began to shout as the boats turned for home, and the whole bay seemed to lean with them.","zh":"赛船那天，码头尽头那根杆子旁边立着一根高高的桅杆。一个男人举着一根长竿升起了旗，帆桁在水面上摆过去。风很冷，像从冰上刮来的一股极地寒流。我表弟第一圈时得把绳子抓牢，还要盯着岸上那盏终端灯。一只鸟飞过来停在杆子顶上，怎么也不肯走。船掉头往回时人群喊了起来，整个海湾好像都跟着它们一起倾倒。"},"project":{"tw":[["projector",4],["figure",0],["offer",3],["draw",2],["build",6],["picture",0],["shoot",3],["imagine",2],["work",6],["plan",2]],"en":"For our class project we had to build a small model of a bridge and show it with a projector. My partner would draw the first picture, then I would shoot a short film of the finished thing. We made a simple plan and divided the work between us. I tried to imagine the weight it could hold, but the figure on the paper looked wrong. The teacher offered to help us fix it before the fair. In the end the model stood, and our little project was the best in the room. Everyone in the class clapped when we turned it on.","zh":"这次班级作业，我们得搭一座小桥梁模型，再用投影仪演示。我搭档先画出第一张图，然后由我拍一段短片，拍成品的样子。我们定了个简单的计划，把活分给两个人。我试着想象它能承多重，可纸上的数字看着不对。老师主动提出在展评前帮我们改一改。最后模型立住了，我们这个小作业是全班最好的。我们把它打开时，全班都鼓了掌。"},"propose":{"tw":[["proposition",4],["offer",3],["move",3],["choose",2],["approve",6],["suggest",0],["advance",3],["plan",2],["implement",6],["advise",0]],"en":"At the morning meeting the manager began to propose a new way of working. His proposition was simple: fewer forms and shorter hours. He would suggest that each team choose one person to speak for the rest. I had to advise him that we could not implement it before the end of the month. My colleague wanted to move the start date and to offer a small trial first. The board did not approve the first plan, but they agreed to advance the second one. In the end we were allowed a short test, and it went well. Nobody in the room was surprised.","zh":"晨会上，经理提出要改一套新的工作方式。他的提议很简单：少点表格，缩短工时。他建议每个小组选一个人替大家发言。我不得不提醒他，这个月底之前推行不了。同事想把开始日期往后挪，先搞个小范围试验。董事会没通过第一版方案，却同意把第二版往前推。最后我们获准试一小段时间，效果还不错。屋里没人觉得意外。"},"provide":{"tw":[["provision",4],["allow",0],["bed",3],["fix",2],["need",6],["leave",0],["date",3],["support",2],["access",6],["offer",0]],"en":"The small hotel would provide a simple room and one meal a day. The provision of hot water was a problem that year, and they had to fix the old boiler twice. Each bed had a date written on the wall above it, and the guests would leave their names below. The owner did not allow pets in the dining room, but she would offer a bowl of milk at the door. She said she wanted to support the families who came back every summer. There was no easy access to the beach, only a long path. For the price, nobody seemed to need more.","zh":"这家小旅馆提供一间简朴的房，一天一顿饭。热水供应那一年成了问题，那台老锅炉他们修了两回。每张床上方都写着日期，客人就在下面留下自己的名字。老板不让宠物进餐厅，但会在门口给一碗牛奶。她说她想帮衬那些每年都回来的家庭。去海滩没有方便的通道，只有一条长路。就这个价钱，好像没人需要更多了。"},"quality":{"tw":[["qualify",4],["choice",0],["register",3],["property",2],["excellent",6],["character",0],["characteristic",3],["attribute",2],["lack",6],["prime",0]],"en":"The old shop sold cloth of the finest quality, and my mother said you could judge it by its feel. The choice was small, but every roll was excellent. The owner would register each sale in a thick book and write down the property of the cloth: its weight, its colour, its character, its every attribute. One characteristic she always looked for was a tight weave. She said a lack of care showed at once. That was the prime reason her shop stayed open when others closed. I had to qualify my own praise, though, because I could not tell good cloth from bad.","zh":"那家老店卖的料子上等，我妈说凭手感就能分辨。可选的种类不多，但每一卷都极好。老板会把每笔买卖记在一本厚册子上，写下料子的性质：分量、颜色、品相，还有每一样特征。她总要找的一个特点是织得紧。她说一疏忽一眼就看得出来。她的店能在别家都关门的时候开着，头一条原因就在这儿。不过我也得给自己的夸赞打个折扣，因为我根本分不出布的好坏。"},"recognize":{"tw":[["recognition",4],["know",2],["wish",3],["accept",2],["regard",6],["realise",0],["identify",3],["address",2],["respect",6],["spot",0]],"en":"I did not recognize my old teacher in the crowd. There was no recognition in my eyes at first, and it took me a moment to realise who she was. She would not accept my apology, but then she laughed. She said she could still identify every student by the way they walked. We stood at the same address for a while and talked about the old days. I had to know how she had been, and she wished me well in return. She said she held me in high regard and hoped I would show the same respect to my own students. Then she pointed to a spot by the door where we had once sat.","zh":"人群里我没认出我那位老师。起初我眼里根本没有认出来，愣了一会儿才想起她是谁。她不肯接受我的道歉，可随后又笑了。她说她还能凭走路的样子认出每一个学生来。我们在同一个地址前站了一会儿，聊起从前的日子。我很想知道她这些年怎么样，她也祝我好。她说她一向看重我，希望我对自己的学生也能给出同样的尊重。然后她指了指门边的一处地方，从前我们曾坐过那儿。"},"refer":{"tw":[["referee",4],["concern",0],["express",3],["mean",2],["instance",6],["mention",0],["involve",3],["send",2],["particular",6],["relate",0]],"en":"In the essay the teacher would refer to a particular book on page ten, and she asked us to relate the idea to our own lives. My concern was simply to express what I really mean. I could mention one instance from my own street, but I was not sure it would help. The referee at the match on Saturday had to send a long note to the school about the rules. He said the case would involve both teams. In the end I wrote about a small thing that had happened at home, and it was enough. The teacher liked it and read it out.","zh":"写这篇作文时，老师会提到某一本书的第十页，还让我们把这个想法联系到自己的生活。我关心的只是把真正想说的表达出来。我可以举我们街上的一件事，可又拿不准它有没有用。周六那场比赛的裁判不得不给学校寄一封长信，讲的是规则。他说这事会牵扯到两队。最后我写了一件家里发生的小事，也就够了。老师很喜欢，还念了出来。"},"pronounce":{"tw":[["pronouncement",4],["say",0],["round",3],["declare",2],["swear",6],["articulate",0],["voice",3],["speak",6],["enunciate",0]],"en":"In drama class the teacher asked me to pronounce each word slowly and to enunciate the ends of them. I had to swear I would not laugh at the others. She would say the lines herself first, then walk round the room and listen. Her voice was low and easy to follow, and every young actor tried to speak the same way. She wanted us to articulate clearly, as if making a public pronouncement. I could not declare the last line without shaking. In the end I managed it, and she smiled. It was only a small victory, but I felt taller.","zh":"戏剧课上，老师让我把每个词慢慢念出来，还要把字尾咬清楚。我得发誓不笑话别人。她先自己把台词念一遍，然后在屋里走一圈，听我们念。她的声音低而清楚，很好跟，每个小演员都想学她那样说话。她要我们把话说利落，像在当众宣告什么。最后一句我怎么也稳不住就念不出来。到头来我还是念完了，她笑了。这只是一次小小的胜利，可我觉得自己高了些。"},"lower":{"tw":[["depress",3],["dip",3],["change",2],["raise",1],["low",6],["frown",0],["incline",3],["move",2],["upper",6],["glower",0]],"en":"The men had to lower the heavy beam slowly into the trench. One of them pushed a button, and the machine began to dip. The change in the ground was small at first, then the whole upper part seemed to move. My uncle would not raise his voice, but a frown crossed his face. A stranger stood at the top of the slope and began to glower at us. The ground had an incline, and it was hard to keep the beam steady. They had to depress the lever to the lowest point. Nobody spoke for a while. It was slow work.","zh":"工人们得把那根沉重的横梁慢慢放进沟里。一个人按了按钮，机器开始往下沉。地面起初只变了一点点，接着上面那一整块好像都动了起来。我叔没有提高嗓门，可眉头皱了一下。一个陌生人在坡顶上站着，开始恶狠狠地瞪我们。地面是斜的，横梁很难扶稳。他们只得把操纵杆压到最低那一档。好一阵没人说话。这活儿干得慢。"},"prove":{"tw":[["raise",2],["control",3],["grow",2],["disprove",1],["doubt",6],["rise",0],["float",3],["inform",2],["test",0]],"en":"In the school lab we had to prove that warm water would rise above cold water. My partner tried to raise the glass slowly and to control the flow. We watched a drop of dye grow and begin to float on the surface. A second test was meant to disprove the first, but it gave the same result. I began to doubt our own numbers. The teacher asked us to inform the class and to write down every step. Nothing in science was certain, she said, until you could show it twice. We did not mind doing the whole thing again.","zh":"在学校实验室里，我们得证明温水会浮在冷水上面。我搭档试着把杯子慢慢抬起，控制住水流。我们看着一滴染料散开、长开来，然后开始浮在表面。第二次实验本来是想推翻第一次的，结果还是一样。我开始怀疑起我们自己的数据。老师要我们把结论讲给全班听，还要把每一步都写下来。她说，科学里什么都说不准，除非你能把它重复两遍。再把整件事做一遍，我们也不嫌麻烦。"},"reduce":{"tw":[["cut",0],["pole",3],["change",2],["gain",1],["increase",6],["concentrate",0],["shave",3],["separate",2],["risk",6],["contract",3]],"en":"The factory wanted to reduce the smoke that left its tall pole each morning. The plan was to cut the waste, change the old burners, and separate the heavy dust from the air. The managers said any gain in clean air would be small at first, and that the cost might increase. They had to concentrate their money on one part of the plant. My uncle said they should shave the budget elsewhere and take the risk. He also had to reduce a short contract with a supplier. In the end the air did get a little cleaner. It was a small change.","zh":"厂里想把每天早上从那根高烟囱冒出去的烟减少一些。办法是少浪费、换掉旧燃烧器，再把重的粉尘从空气里分出来。管理层说，空气能干净多少，起先也许很有限，而且花费可能还要涨。他们只能把资金集中花在厂里的一处。我叔说，别的开支该砍就砍，这风险得冒。他还得缩减一份跟供货商的短期合同。最后空气确实干净了一点。变化不大。"},"remain":{"tw":[["remainder",4],["continue",0],["stand",3],["remnant",4],["rest",0],["stick",3],["stay",0]],"en":"After the fire only a few walls would remain of the old house. A single chimney continued to stand, and a dark remnant of the roof still stuck out above it. The rest was ash and black stone. My aunt said she would continue to visit the place each year, and that a small part of the family would always stay with it. The remainder of the land she gave to the village. We stood there for a long while without speaking. Then we walked back down the lane. The wind moved in the trees.","zh":"那栋老屋烧过之后，只剩几堵墙还立着。一根烟囱照旧竖着，屋顶的一块黑洞洞的残件还从上面探出来。其余的都是灰和黑石头。我姑妈说她会每年继续来看这个地方，家里总有一个人会一直跟它待在一起。剩下的地她给了村里。我们在那儿站了很久，谁也没说话。然后我们沿着小路走了回去。树间的风在动。"},"resist":{"tw":[["stand",3],["strike",3],["fight",2],["surrender",1],["suppress",6],["protest",0],["demonstrate",3],["oppose",2],["abandon",6],["refuse",0]],"en":"The workers decided to resist the new rules, and they would not surrender without a word. They began to stand outside the gate and to protest in a quiet way. One group would demonstrate in the square, while another chose to strike for two days. The owner tried to suppress the whole thing, but he could not oppose ten people alone. My father refused to abandon his friends, and he would fight for a fair wage. In the end both sides agreed to meet again on Monday. Nobody had won yet, and both sides were tired. The gate stayed shut for the rest of the day.","zh":"工人们决定抵制新规定，说什么也不肯一声不响就认输。他们开始站在大门外，静静地抗议。一拨人要在广场上示威，另一拨人则选择罢工两天。老板想把这事压下去，可他一个人没法跟十个人对着干。我爸不肯丢下朋友，他要为一份公道的工钱争一争。最后双方答应周一再谈。谁也没赢，两边都累坏了。那天余下的时候，大门一直关着。"},"medicine":{"tw":[["medical",4],["medication",0],["remedy",3],["drug",2],["study",6],["hygiene",3],["treat",2],["institute",6]],"en":"My grandmother kept her medicine in a small box by the bed, and she knew each pill by name. The medical student who lived upstairs would study with her in the evening and explain how each drug worked. He said good hygiene was often a better remedy than any tablet, though her medication still mattered. She would treat the whole family with tea and quiet advice before she reached for the box. A doctor from a nearby institute came once a month to check on her. She said the best medicine was a warm room and someone to talk to. That was enough for her.","zh":"我奶奶把她的药放在床边一个小盒子里，每一粒叫什么她都清楚。住在楼上的那个学医的学生晚上会来跟她一起看书，讲每种药是怎么起作用的。他说讲究卫生常常比哪片药都管用，不过她的药也还是不能停。她总是先用茶和几句轻声的劝慰招呼全家人，然后才去伸手拿那个盒子。附近一个研究院的大夫每月来一次，看看她的情况。她说，最好的药就是一间暖屋子，还有一个能说话的人。对她来说，这就够了。"},"nerve":{"tw":[["nervous",4],["face",0],["courage",2],["brain",6],["heart",0],["brace",2],["stomach",6],["steel",0]],"en":"My brother had to ask the bank to wait another month, and it took real nerve. His face stayed calm, but I could see his nervous hands under the table. He had found the courage somewhere and walked in alone. His brain had gone over the numbers all night, his heart was beating fast, and his stomach felt tight and cold. He would brace himself each time the door opened. The manager was a man of steel and said no at first. Still, my brother held his ground and explained every line again, and in the end they gave him the extra time.","zh":"我哥得去求银行再宽限一个月，这得有真正的胆量。他脸上很平静，可我看见桌子底下他发抖的手。他不知从哪儿找来的勇气，一个人走了进去。他脑子里整夜都在算那些数字，心怦怦直跳，胃里又紧又凉。每次门一响，他都要先给自己打气。经理是个铁石心肠的人，一开始说了不行。可我哥没退，把每一条又解释了一遍，最后还是争来了那点时间。"},"option":{"tw":[["opt",4],["choice",0],["decision",3],["deal",6],["pick",0],["vote",3],["allow",6],["alternative",0]],"en":"When the old car finally died, we had only one real option left, and nobody wanted to make the decision alone. My father said we could pick any car we liked, but he would not allow us to spend more than we had. My mother wanted a small one; he preferred a deal on a bigger one. We took a vote at the kitchen table, and in the end we opted for the cheapest of the three. There was no other alternative that fit our street and our budget. I still think we made the wrong choice, but the car still runs.","zh":"那辆旧车终于报废时，我们只剩一个真正的选项，可谁都不愿独自做这个决定。我爸说车随我们挑，但不许花超过手头的钱。我妈想要小的，他看中了一辆大一点、划算的。我们在饭桌上投了票，最后选了那三辆里最便宜的。再没有别的选择既适合我们这条街又符合预算。我到现在还觉得这个选择不对，不过车还能开。"},"pleasure":{"tw":[["please",4],["delight",3],["comfort",3],["choice",2],["pain",1],["luck",6],["joy",0],["thrill",6]],"en":"Nothing gave my grandmother more pleasure than her small garden in June. She would say it was a delight to watch the first roses open, and she took comfort in the long evenings there. She had never had a choice about the hard years of her life, but she had this, and it was enough. There was some pain in her knees, yet she still knelt by the beds. Good luck with the weather, she would say, is half of joy. The real thrill for her was a single white flower that opened once a year. She would please herself by sitting there until dark.","zh":"没有什么比我奶奶六月里那片小花园更让她快活的了。她总说，看着头一批玫瑰绽开是一种喜悦，长长的傍晚也让她觉得安慰。她这辈子那些苦日子从来由不得她挑，可她有这片园子，就够了。膝盖是有些疼，可她还是跪在花垄边。她常说，天气上运气好，快乐就有一半。真正让她激动的是每年只开一朵的那种白花。她愿意坐在那儿一直坐到天黑，就为了让自己高兴。"},"prime":{"tw":[["primer",4],["choice",0],["fill",2],["minister",6],["flower",0],["fix",2],["cabinet",6],["ground",0]],"en":"The old cabinet had been in the family for years, and in its prime it held the best plates. My uncle decided to fix it himself one winter, working slowly whenever the light was good. He filled every crack with a primer first, then painted the whole thing. The ground under it was worn, so he moved it near the window. In the flower season my aunt would put a choice of fresh stems on top. A minister once came to the house and said the room looked best in that corner. I still think that cabinet was the true prime of the place.","zh":"那只旧柜子在咱家放了好多年，最好的盘子以前都搁在里面，那正是它最风光的时候。有一年冬天我叔决定自己修，光线好的时候就慢慢弄。他先用底漆把每道缝都填上，再整个刷了一遍。柜子底下的地面磨旧了，他就把它挪到窗边。到了花季，我婶会在柜顶摆上几枝挑好的新花。有回一位牧师来家里，说这屋子就那个角落最好看。我到现在还觉得，那只柜子才是这地方真正的精华。"},"labour":{"tw":[["dig",0],["hunt",3],["class",2],["liberal",6],["drive",0],["effort",3],["fight",2],["party",6],["push",0]],"en":"The labour on the new wall took the whole of August, and my father did most of it himself. He would dig the base by hand and push the stones into place one by one, with great effort. My brother would hunt for the smoothest stones along the stream. A small party of neighbours came to help on the last day. One of them, a liberal man with a good heart, would drive his lorry up with the cement. There was no class in that group, and no fight over who would do what. They worked until dark, and then they ate together in the yard. I learned what real work means that summer.","zh":"砌那道新墙的活儿干了整整八月，大半是我爸一个人干的。他会用手挖地基，再把石头一块块推到位，费了很大气力。我弟弟会沿着溪边去找最光溜的石头。最后一天，一小拨邻居来帮忙。其中一个心地厚道、为人慷慨的人，把卡车拉着水泥开上来了。那伙人里不分什么高低，也没人为谁干什么吵。他们一直干到天黑，然后一起在院子里吃饭。那个夏天我明白了什么叫真正的干活。"},"leap":{"tw":[["jump",2],["burst",3],["move",2],["climb",6],["spring",0],["hop",3],["increase",2],["finish",6],["bounce",3]],"en":"My sister would leap from stone to stone across the stream without ever falling in. She could jump higher than any of us and would not stop until she reached the far bank. From there she had to climb a low wall and then move along the top like a bird. In spring the water would burst over the stones, and the level would increase quickly. She would hop back the other way, laughing, and bounce on the grass at the end. One day she slipped, and it was the finish of our game for a week. I have never seen anyone leap like her.","zh":"我妹妹能从一块石头跳到另一块，横过小溪，一次都没掉下去。她跳得比我们谁都高，不到对岸绝不停下。到了那边她还得爬上一道矮墙，再像鸟一样沿着墙头走。春天一到，水会漫过石头，水位涨得飞快。她会笑着从原路蹦回来，最后在草地上弹两下。有一天她滑了一跤，我们这个玩法就停了一个星期。我从没见过谁像她那样跳。"},"limit":{"tw":[["fix",0],["edge",3],["choose",2],["minimum",6],["boundary",2],["rule",3],["control",2],["maximum",6],["confine",0]],"en":"The sign at the edge of the pool gave a clear limit: no more than ten children at a time. The teacher had to control the gate and choose who would go in first. There was a rule about the maximum depth, and a minimum age of six. A low wall marked the boundary between the shallow end and the deep one. If we broke it, the pool would fix a new lock and we would all lose the hour. Sometimes a child would try to confine the game to one corner, and the rest would complain. The limit was there for a reason, and we learned to respect it.","zh":"泳池边的牌子上写着清清楚楚的限度：一次最多十个孩子。老师得把着入口，决定谁先进去。关于最深水位有规定，最小年龄是六岁。一道矮墙标出浅水区和深水区的分界。要是我们犯规，泳池就会换个新锁，我们那一小时就都没了。有时会有孩子想把游戏限制在一个角里，别人就不乐意。这个限度是有道理的，我们也学着尊重它。"},"loose":{"tw":[["easy",0],["run",3],["change",2],["tight",1],["stick",6],["free",5],["bail",3],["apart",6],["light",5]],"en":"One screw on my bicycle had come loose, and the whole wheel began to move from side to side. My father said it was an easy fault to fix, but I had to do it myself. He would not let me run to the shop for a new part. He showed me how to hold the nut tight and how to stick a small card between the spokes. A loose chain can change the way a machine feels, he said, and it can come apart on a hill. He gave me a free afternoon and a light to work by. I had to bail the water out of the bucket first, and it was dirty work.","zh":"我自行车上一颗螺丝松了，整个轮子开始左右晃。我爸说这毛病好修，可得我自己动手。他不让我跑去店里买新零件。他教我怎么把螺母拧紧，怎么在辐条之间塞一张小卡片。他说链条一松，机器的感觉就变了，上坡时还可能散架。他给了我一个空闲的下午和一盏灯让我干活。我得先把桶里的水舀出去，这活儿很脏。"},"mask":{"tw":[["disguise",2],["camouflage",3],["cover",2],["tattoo",6],["cloak",0],["domino",3],["hide",2],["helmet",6],["masquerade",3]],"en":"At the school play every child had to wear a mask, and mine was a plain white one that covered the whole face. My mother would help me disguise my voice as well, so nobody would know me on stage. We used a little camouflage paint on the back of the neck, where the mask did not reach. Someone had drawn a domino pattern on a cloak for the older boy, and he would hide behind it until his turn. A girl wore a small helmet and a fake tattoo on her arm. It was a masquerade, but for one evening we were all someone else. I have kept my mask ever since.","zh":"学校的演出上每个孩子都得戴面具，我那个是张素白的，把整张脸都盖住。我妈还帮我把嗓音也伪装起来，这样台上就没人认得出我。我们在脖子上涂了点迷彩颜料，面具够不到那儿。有人给那个大点的男孩在一件斗篷上画了多米诺的花样，他会躲在后面等到自己上场。一个女孩戴着小头盔，胳膊上贴了个假纹身。那是一场假面舞会，可那一晚我们都成了别人。那张面具我留到了现在。"},"mass":{"tw":[["deal",0],["press",3],["crowd",2],["wave",6],["lot",0],["flood",3],["magnitude",2],["cause",6],["mess",0]],"en":"By evening a mass of papers covered my desk, and the pile seemed to grow while I watched. A deal had come in that morning, and with it a whole flood of files. My colleague would press me to sign each one without reading, but I refused. The crowd of figures on the page began to blur. A wave of tiredness came over me. I tried to work out the magnitude of the mistake we were about to make. There was a lot to sort, and the mess was not only on paper. The real cause was a meeting nobody had written down. I stayed until nine and left the rest for Monday.","zh":"到傍晚，我桌上堆满了一大堆文件，眼看着还在往上长。早上来了笔生意，跟着来的是一整批卷宗。同事一直催我别细看就签字，我拒绝了。纸上密密麻麻的数字开始发花。一阵倦意涌上来。我想算清楚我们正要犯的错有多大。要理的东西太多了，乱的不只是纸上这些。真正的起因是一次没人记录下来的会。我干到九点，剩下的留到周一。"},"match":{"tw":[["agree",0],["final",3],["change",2],["round",6],["catch",0],["look",3],["family",2],["tournament",6],["check",0]],"en":"On the morning of the match my father and I could not agree about anything, from the route to the team. It was the final of a small local tournament, and the whole family was coming. The ground was wet, and they had to check the pitch twice before they let us in. In the second round our best player had to come off with a bad knee. I could not catch what the coach was shouting. My mother, who never watched football, spent the game looking at the crowd. The score did not change after that, and we walked home in the rain.","zh":"比赛那天早上，我爸跟我没一样谈得拢，从走哪条路到上谁上场。那是一个本地小赛事的决赛，全家都要来。场地是湿的，他们查了两遍才放我们进去。第二轮里我们最厉害的球员膝盖受了伤，只能下场。教练喊什么我也听不真切。我妈从不看球，整场都在看人。那以后比分就没再变过，我们冒着雨走回了家。"},"mate":{"tw":[["couple",0],["husband",3],["beat",2],["succeed",6],["fellow",0],["ride",3],["join",2],["incumbent",6],["pair",0]],"en":"Every Friday my father would ride to the chess club and join the same three friends at the back table. He had learned the game from his own mate, a fellow who had worked beside him for years. The incumbent champion was a quiet woman whose husband kept the score. My mother said the two of them were like a couple, the way they would beat the board with their fingers and laugh. To succeed there you had to lose a hundred times first. I asked to join once, but I was too slow. Each player had to bring a pair of clocks.","zh":"每个星期五，我爸都会骑车去棋社，跟后桌那三个老熟人坐到一起。这棋是他从自己那位老搭档那儿学的，那人跟他共事了好些年。守擂的冠军是个安静的女人，记分的是她丈夫。我妈说他们俩像一对老夫老妻，手指敲着棋盘边笑边说。想在那儿出头，你先得输上一百回。我曾要求入伙，可我太慢了。每个棋手都得自己带一副棋钟。"},"material":{"tw":[["real",0],["paper",3],["substance",2],["immaterial",1],["contain",6],["stuff",0],["waste",3],["content",6],["cloth",0]],"en":"The material my aunt used for her curtains was a thick cloth from the old mill, real wool, nothing fancy. She would hold it against the light to check the substance before she cut. The price seemed high at first, but she said the number was immaterial next to the wear. Each roll had a paper note inside, and she would read the content before she began. Nothing was wasted; the stuff left over became cushions. I asked her where she had learned to sew, and she said from her mother, in a room with no heating. She could contain a whole winter's cold in that small workshop.","zh":"我姑姑做窗帘用的料子，是旧厂子出的一种厚布，真羊毛的，不花哨。她会把布对着光看看质地，才下剪子。价钱一开始看着贵，她说比起耐穿，那个数字根本不算什么。每卷布里都夹着一张纸条，她动手前会先看看上面写着什么。一点都没浪费，剩下的料做了坐垫。我问她跟谁学的针线，她说是跟她妈学的，在一间没有暖气的屋子里。她能在那个小作坊里扛住一整个冬天的冷。"},"melt":{"tw":[["run",0],["try",3],["change",2],["crust",6],["fade",0],["fuse",3],["blend",2],["chill",6],["dissolve",2]],"en":"By March the snow on the roof had begun to melt, and the water ran down the wall all day. My father would try to clear the gutter before the ice could fuse the pipe shut. At night the crust on top would harden again, and the cold would chill the whole house. He said the colours of the sky would change and fade and blend as the spring came on. A lump of salt would dissolve in a bucket by the door. He would run his hand along the ice to see how thin it had grown. It was the same every year, and he never tired of watching it.","zh":"到了三月，屋顶上的雪开始化，水整天顺着墙往下淌。我爸会赶在冰把水管冻死之前把檐槽清一清。夜里表面那层硬壳又会结起来，寒气渗进整座房子。他说随着春天到来，天色会一点点褪去又混成新的颜色。门口桶里的一块盐会慢慢化开。他会用手顺着冰摸过去，看看薄到什么程度了。年年都是这样，他看多少回都不腻。"},"minor":{"tw":[["kid",0],["orphan",3],["juvenile",2],["major",1],["string",6],["small",0],["peanut",5],["result",6],["fry",0]],"en":"Near the market, a small stall hired a kid to fry peanuts in a deep pan of oil. He was a minor, so the owner asked his aunt to sign a paper, because the boy was an orphan with no parents left. A juvenile rule said he could stay only until dark. The result was a long wait for the woman who ran the stand. Her major worry was the heat of the oil. She taught him to string the nuts on a thin line and dip them one by one. By evening the pan was empty and the small bag of coins felt heavy in his hand.","zh":"市场边上，一个小摊雇了个孩子，在深油锅里炸花生。因为他是未成年人，摊主要他姑姑签一张纸，那孩子父母都没了，是个孤儿。按规定少年只能干到天黑。结果老板娘等了好久。她最担心的是油温。她教他把花生用细线串起来，一颗一颗放下去。到了傍晚，锅空了，他手里那一小袋硬币沉甸甸的。"},"mix":{"tw":[["combine",0],["cut",3],["add",2],["taste",6],["blend",3],["melt",3],["change",2],["hot",6],["integrate",0]],"en":"My aunt let me mix the cake batter while she cut the fruit. I had to add the sugar slowly, then combine and blend it with the butter until the colour began to change. The room was hot, and the chocolate would melt if I left it near the stove. She told me to taste it before the last spoon, then integrate the dry flour with the wet part in a slow circle. The final mix was smooth, and it smelled of lemon. When the oven door opened, the whole kitchen filled with steam. We let the tin cool on the windowsill before we ate.","zh":"姑姑让我拌蛋糕糊，她在一旁切水果。我得慢慢加糖，再把它和黄油拌到一起，直到颜色开始变。厨房里很热，巧克力放在炉子边上就会化。她让我在最后一勺前尝尝，再把干面粉和湿的部分慢慢转着拌匀。拌好的糊很细，一股柠檬味。烤箱门一开，整个厨房都是蒸汽。我们把烤盘放在窗台上晾凉才吃。"},"model":{"tw":[["sit",0],["figure",3],["shape",2],["design",6],["pattern",3],["original",3],["expose",2],["prototype",6],["pose",0]],"en":"A small model of a bridge sits on the table, cut from thin wood. My brother had drawn the design first, then built a rough prototype to test the shape. He would expose it to a lamp to see the shadows, and he liked to pose it at different angles. The pattern on the paper was only a guide. The original figure of the plan, a tiny man, stood at the end of the rail. It looked right, so he began the real one. When the glue dried, he put the model on the shelf beside the finished work.","zh":"桌上放着一座小桥模型，是薄木片削成的。弟弟先画好设计，又做了个粗糙的原型来试形状。他会把它举到灯下看影子，喜欢摆成不同的角度。纸上的图案只是个参考。原图里的小人立在栏杆尽头。看着对了，他才动手做真件。胶水干了，他把模型放到架子上，挨着做好的活儿。"},"mount":{"tw":[["climb",0],["grey",3],["fix",2],["ridge",6],["mountain",0],["jump",3],["horse",2],["hill",6],["ride",3]],"en":"A grey horse stood ready at the foot of the hill. My uncle would ride up along the ridge before the light changed, and he liked to fix the saddle himself. The mountain behind us was still in cloud. He said a good mount knows the path better than the rider. At the steep part we had to climb slowly, and once the animal made a short jump over a stone. From the top we could see the whole valley. He let me hold the reins on the way down, and my hands were still shaking when we reached the gate.","zh":"一匹灰马站在山脚下等着。叔叔总爱趁天光未变时沿着山脊骑上去，还喜欢自己修马鞍。身后的山还裹在云里。他说好马比骑手更认路。到陡的地方我们只能慢慢爬，那牲口还一度跳过一块石头。到了顶上，整条山谷都在眼前。下山时他让我抓着缰绳，到门口时我的手还在抖。"},"nail":{"tw":[["complete",0],["spike",3],["hit",2],["knife",6],["ace",0],["tack",3],["pass",2],["glue",6],["arrest",0]],"en":"He wanted to complete the wooden frame before lunch, so he took a nail and a heavy hammer. The first hit bent the metal, and he had to pull it out with a knife. He used a small tack instead, then a long spike for the corner, and passed the glue to his helper. A boy who was an ace with tools showed him how to hold the board. Later, a police car came down the lane to arrest a man two doors away, and the noise stopped all the work. By evening the frame hung straight, and nobody mentioned the car.","zh":"他想在午饭前把木框做完，就拿起一根铁钉和一把重锤。第一下就把钉子敲弯了，他只好用刀把它撬出来。他换了一枚小图钉，角落里又用了根长钉，然后把胶水递给帮手。一个使工具很在行的小伙子教他怎么扶住木板。后来巷子里来了辆警车，抓走了隔两家住的男人，干活的声音全停了。到傍晚，框子挂得笔直，谁也没再提那辆车。"},"organize":{"tw":[["form",0],["lay",3],["join",2],["participate",6],["prepare",0],["mount",3],["manage",2],["disrupt",6],["direct",0]],"en":"Our class had to organize a small show for the school. We would form three groups, and each one had to prepare a short scene. My sister helped lay out the chairs, and she asked me to join the singing part. I did not want to participate at first, but she could manage me better than anyone. A late storm might disrupt the plan, so we moved everything under the roof. The teacher gave a direct order: no one leaves before the last act. In the end we managed to mount it on time.","zh":"我们班得为学校组织一场小演出。要分成三组，每组准备一个短剧。姐姐帮着摆椅子，还让我加入合唱。我一开始不想参加，可她管我比谁都管得住。一场迟来的暴雨可能打乱计划，我们就把东西都挪到了屋檐下。老师直接下令：最后一幕演完谁也不许走。最后我们总算按时把这台戏办起来了。"},"pattern":{"tw":[["figure",0],["fashion",3],["plan",2],["characteristic",6],["form",0],["scale",3],["match",2],["similar",6],["normal",0]],"en":"The cloth on the table had a simple pattern of grey lines. My mother said that kind of form was out of fashion, yet the colour seemed right. She had a plan to cut it into a skirt, and she checked the scale of every square with a ruler. I noticed a characteristic in her work: she would hold the cloth up, look at it, and put it down again. She wanted the two sides to match. The result was similar to a picture in an old book. Nothing about it looked normal, and that was the point. While she worked, she would figure the cost of the cloth aloud.","zh":"桌上的布只有简单的灰色线条图案。妈妈说这种样式早过时了，可颜色看着顺眼。她打算把它裁成一条裙子，还用尺子量了每个方格的尺寸。我发现她干活有个特点：把布举起来看看，又放下。她想让两片布对齐。成品像一本旧书里的插图。它看上去一点也不寻常，而这正是她要的。她一边干，一边把布料的价钱大声算出来。"},"pin":{"tw":[["fall",0],["rivet",3],["leg",2],["bow",6],["stick",0],["brooch",3],["attack",2],["rope",6],["flag",0]],"en":"A pin fell from the table and rolled under the chair. My grandmother was mending a coat, and she used a brooch to hold the cloth instead of a rope of thread. Her leg was stiff that day, so she asked me to pick it up. A small flag hung on the wall, held by a stick. She said a sharp attack of wind could pull the window open, and the bow on her dress would come loose. Then she took a rivet tool and fixed the handle of the box. It was a quiet afternoon.","zh":"一枚大头针从桌上掉下去，滚到椅子底下。奶奶在补一件外套，用一枚胸针别住布料，没用线绳。她那天腿发僵，就让我去捡。墙上挂着一面小旗，靠一根棍子支着。她说一阵猛风能把窗户吹开，她裙子上的蝴蝶结也会松开。后来她拿铆钉工具修好了箱子的提手。那是个安静的下午。"},"pink":{"tw":[["knock",0],["coral",3],["cut",2],["purple",6],["tap",0],["carnation",3],["flower",2],["blue",6],["rap",0]],"en":"The sky over the yard was pink. My neighbour cut a flower for the table, a red carnation, and set it in a glass. The curtain by the window was purple, and the light made the blue wall look warm. Someone gave a light tap at the door, then a louder knock, and I heard a rap on the glass. I thought of the coral she kept in a small box, a soft colour like the evening. Nobody came in. I stood still and watched the garden go dark, and the flowers by the wall closed for the night.","zh":"院子上的天空是粉红的。邻居剪了一朵花摆到桌上，一朵红石竹，插在玻璃杯里。窗边的帘子是紫的，灯光把蓝墙照得发暖。有人在门上轻敲了一下，接着敲得更响，我又听见玻璃上啪的一声。我想起她收在小盒子里的珊瑚，那颜色像黄昏一样柔。没有人进来。我站着不动，看着园子暗下去，墙边的花也都合上了。"},"pitch":{"tw":[["sky",0],["ball",3],["deal",2],["game",6],["deliver",0],["camp",3],["hit",2],["straight",6],["flip",0]],"en":"A boy stood on the dry grass and began to pitch the ball to his sister. The game was simple: hit it straight and run. They had set up a camp at the back of the field, with a tent so old that its poles leaned at a strange pitch. I had to deal with the rope while they played. Once the ball went over the wall, and she had to deliver it back with a wide throw. Then the sky turned grey and we packed up. A quick flip of the wrist, and the last ball landed in the bag.","zh":"一个男孩站在干草地上，开始把球扔给妹妹。游戏很简单：打直了就跑。他们在场地后头搭了个营地，那顶帐篷太旧，杆子斜得厉害。他们玩的时候我得去弄那根绳子。有一次球飞过了墙，她只好使劲扔回来。后来天变灰了，我们就收东西。手腕一抖，最后一个球落进了袋子。"},"plain":{"tw":[["apparent",0],["flat",3],["land",2],["fancy",1],["thick",6],["field",0],["report",3],["coat",6],["kick",0]],"en":"The plain behind the town is wide and flat. In winter the land there is hard, and the grass grows thick along the road. A farmer in a heavy coat crossed the field with a plastic bag. It was apparent that he did not want company. He gave a small kick to a stone and walked on. Later a report in the local paper said the council would build there, and a fancy map showed a new road across the open ground. I hope they leave it plain. For now the wind still moves the grass all the way to the river.","zh":"镇子后面的平原又宽又平。冬天那儿的土地很硬，路边的草长得又厚又密。一个穿厚外套的农民提着塑料袋穿过田野，看得出来他不想有人陪。他踢了一下石子，接着往前走。后来当地报纸上一份报告说，镇里打算在那儿动工，一张花哨的图上画着一条穿过空地的新路。但愿他们别去动它。眼下，风还把草一路吹到河边。"},"plane":{"tw":[["flat",0],["jet",3],["cut",2],["flight",6],["shave",0],["amphibian",3],["shape",2],["aboard",6],["sheet",0]],"en":"We watched the plane climb above the flat fields. It was a small jet, and the shape of its wing cut the pale sky. My uncle said an amphibian could land on water as well as on land, and that this one had a long flight ahead. He would shave before he left and take one clean sheet of paper for his notes. Later he went aboard through a narrow door. The whole machine was smaller than I had expected, like a toy that had grown a little. Its engines made a low sound, like a door opening somewhere far away.","zh":"我们看着飞机升到平坦的田野上空。那是架小喷气机，机翼的形状切开了发白的天。叔叔说水陆两用机能落在水上，也能落在陆地上，还说这架要飞很远。他出发前会刮净胡子，带一张干净纸做笔记。后来他从一扇窄门上了机。整架机器比我想的小，像个长大了点的玩具。它的引擎发出低低的声音，像远处有扇门被推开。"},"plate":{"tw":[["home",0],["bridge",3],["base",2],["bottom",6],["scale",0],["silver",3],["coat",2],["spoon",6],["shell",0]],"en":"A silver plate stood at the bottom of the shelf, under a heavy coat of dust. My mother brought it home from her mother, along with a small spoon and a shell she had found by a bridge. She would wash the base of it and set it on the scale to weigh the flour for bread. I liked the thin line of blue around its edge. That evening she filled it with hot rice and put it in the middle of the table. We ate from it for years, and it never lost its shine.","zh":"一只银盘放在架子最下层，落了一层厚厚的灰。妈妈把它从外婆家带回来，还带了一把小勺和她在桥边捡到的一只贝壳。她会把盘底洗净，放到秤上称做面包的面粉。我喜欢它边上一道细细的蓝线。那天晚上她盛了热米饭，摆在桌子中间。我们用这只盘子吃了好多年，它一直没失去光泽。"},"pool":{"tw":[["pond",0],["trust",3],["lake",2],["open",6],["consortium",0],["mere",3],["share",2],["spot",6],["syndicate",0]],"en":"Behind the old house there is a pool the size of a small pond, fed by a stream from the lake. The water is open to the sky, and on a hot day it is the best spot in the garden. Three families share it and pay a small sum each year, so in a sense we are a little consortium, almost a syndicate. We trust one another to keep the gate shut. I never liked the word. The children do not care who owns it. They jump in and swim to the far side. For them it is a mere puddle, and that is enough.","zh":"老房子后面有个池子，大小像个池塘，水是从湖里流过来的。水面敞着天，热天里它是园子里最好的地方。三家人合用，每年各出一小笔钱，说起来算个小联合体，几乎像个辛迪加。我们彼此信得过，都会把门关好。我从不喜欢这个词。孩子们才不管归谁。他们跳进去，游到对岸。对他们来说那不过是个水洼，这就够了。"},"pour":{"tw":[["stream",0],["sheet",3],["move",2],["skim",6],["swarm",0],["spill",3],["rain",2],["boil",6],["pelt",0]],"en":"The rain began to pour on the tin roof, and a thin stream ran down the glass. My mother had to move the pots from the yard before the water reached them. I watched a swarm of small insects skim over the surface of the barrel. A sheet of paper blew off the table and landed in the wet grass. The kettle started to boil. Then the sky opened and seemed to pelt the house with stones. Nothing could spill, but the floor was soon dark with water. By morning the yard smelled of clean earth.","zh":"雨开始往铁皮屋顶上倒，一道细流顺着玻璃往下淌。妈妈得赶在水漫过来之前把院子里的盆挪开。我看见一群小虫在水缸面上轻轻掠过。一张纸被风吹下桌子，落进湿草里。水壶开始响了。接着天像裂开一样，仿佛拿石头砸这房子。什么也没洒出来，可地板很快就积了一片黑水。到早上，院子里一股干净的泥土味。"},"pressure":{"tw":[["force",2],["drive",3],["push",2],["ease",6],["press",4],["head",3],["influence",2],["move",6],["squeeze",0]],"en":"The doctor put a hand on my father's shoulder and felt for his pulse. The pressure of her fingers was light but firm. She said his work was the main force behind his trouble, and that he should ease the load on his heart. She told him not to push himself so hard. He had to drive less, sleep more, and stop letting the head of the office press him for answers. Her influence was quiet, and by spring he could walk without a stop. He said he felt the squeeze in his chest only when he moved too fast. He listened to her, which was rare.","zh":"医生把手放在爸爸肩上，摸他的脉。她手指按下去不重，却很稳。她说他的工作是他这毛病的主要推手，他该给心脏减轻负担。她叫他别那么逼自己。他得少开车、多睡觉，别再让办公室的头儿催着要答案。她的影响是无声的，到了春天他走一段路都不用停。他说，只有走得太急时，胸口才会有那种被挤住的感觉。他听了她的话，这很难得。"},"print":{"tw":[["mark",0],["letter",3],["photograph",2],["paper",6],["impress",0],["line",3],["write",2],["magazine",6],["publish",0]],"en":"In the small shop at the corner they print names on paper while you wait. The owner takes a letter from the box, sets it in the frame, and makes a dark mark on the page. He can also print a photograph from your phone, or a short line of text for a card. I asked him for a page with my own words, something I wanted to write for my sister. He said he would publish a small magazine of such pages one day. The result did not impress me at first, but it was mine.","zh":"街角那家小店里，他们能当着你的面把名字印在纸上。店主从盒子里取一个字母，装进框里，在纸上压出一个深色的印子。他还能把你手机里的照片印出来，或者在卡片上印一行字。我请他给我印一页我自己的话，那是我写给我妹妹的。他说有一天要出一本印着这种小页的杂志。印出来的东西起初并没让我多喜欢，可它是我的。"},"process":{"tw":[["serve",0],["rule",3],["manage",2],["step",6],["treat",0],["till",3],["walk",2],["mechanism",6],["work",0]],"en":"Making bread here is a slow process, and my aunt follows the same rules every time. She has to serve the family at seven, so she starts before light. She will till the dough with her hands, then let it rest. The next step is the salt, and after that the long wait. She says you cannot manage bread by force, only by time. The whole mechanism is simple: flour, water, salt, heat, and work. While it bakes, she likes to walk in the yard and treat herself to a quiet cup of tea.","zh":"在我们这儿做面包是个慢活儿，姑姑每次都照同一套规矩来。她七点得开饭，所以天没亮就动手。她用手揉面，再让面醒着。下一步是加盐，之后就慢慢等。她说面包不能靠蛮劲，只能靠时间。整个过程很简单：面粉、水、盐、火，还有工夫。面包烤着的时候，她喜欢到院子里走走，犒劳自己喝杯安静的茶。"},"progress":{"tw":[["build",0],["climb",3],["travel",2],["regress",1],["step",6],["advance",0],["edge",3],["develop",2],["focus",6]],"en":"My reading made slow progress that year. I would build one small habit at a time, and each step felt like a climb on a cold morning. My teacher said a mind can travel far but can also regress if you stop for long. So I tried to advance a little every night, sitting at the edge of the lamp light. I wanted to develop a focus that did not break. By June I could finish a whole book, and the words no longer slid past me. It was not much, but it was mine.","zh":"那一年我读书进步很慢。我一次只养成一个小习惯，每走一步都像在冷早晨往上爬。老师说脑子能跑得很远，可要停久了也会退步。所以我每晚都努力往前挪一点，坐在灯光的边缘。我想练出一种不散的专注。到六月，我能读完一整本书了，那些词也不再从眼前滑过去。这算不了什么，可它是我自己的。"},"punch":{"tw":[["plug",0],["cup",3],["blow",2],["bite",6],["lick",0],["hook",3],["hit",2],["ball",6],["poke",0]],"en":"My father kept a punch in the drawer beside a heavy plug of metal. He would hit it once with a small hammer to make a clean hole in a belt. The blow had to be straight, or the tool would bite the leather and tear it. Once he used the hook of a bent nail instead, and it was a poor poke at best. He poured tea in a cup, took a slow lick of the steam, and went back to work. The long ball of string on the shelf was for tying the parcels.","zh":"爸爸抽屉里有个打孔器，旁边放着一坨很重的金属块。他会用小锤子敲一下，在皮带上打出一个干净的孔。敲下去必须是直的，不然工具会咬住皮子把它扯坏。有一回他改用弯钉子的钩子，那顶多算乱捅一下。他倒了杯茶，慢慢舔了口热气，又回去干活。架子上那团长长的线绳是捆包裹用的。"},"purpose":{"tw":[["use",0],["mind",3],["decide",2],["basic",6],["design",0],["view",3],["goal",2],["essential",6],["intent",0]],"en":"The purpose of the old shed was never clear to me. In my father's mind it had one use: to hold wood. But my mother had a different view, and in spring she decided to clean it out. The basic design was simple, four walls and a tin roof, and the goal was to make a small room for study. She said a window was essential. I do not think that was her true intent at the start. She only wanted somewhere quiet, and the wood could go anywhere. Now she reads there every evening, and the shed smells of paper.","zh":"那间旧棚子到底有什么用，我一直没弄明白。在我爸心里它只有一个用途：堆木料。可我妈看法不同，春天的时候她决定把它清出来。它本来就四堵墙加铁皮顶，很简单，目标是把这儿弄成一间小书房。她说窗户是必须有的。我想她一开始真正的心思不止于此。她只是想要个安静的地方，木料放哪儿都行。现在她每晚都在那儿看书，棚子里一股纸味。"},"quit":{"tw":[["stop",0],["break",3],["leave",2],["talk",6],["cease",0],["drop",3],["abandon",2],["stay",6],["resign",0]],"en":"My cousin decided to quit her job at the factory in March. She did not want to leave in anger, so she gave a month's notice. The manager asked her to stay, and they had a long talk by the gate. She said the noise never ceased, not even at break, and she could not bear it anymore. He offered a lighter post, but she chose to resign and stop for a while. It was hard to abandon the pay. She went home and dropped onto the sofa, and for the first time in years she slept well.","zh":"我表姐三月决定辞掉厂里的工作。她不想带着火气走，就提前一个月打了招呼。经理让她留下，两人在门口聊了很久。她说那噪音连休息时都不停，她再也受不了了。他提出给她换个轻省的岗位，可她还是选择辞职，先停一阵。放弃那份工资不容易。她回到家，一屁股坐到沙发上，这些年头一次睡了个好觉。"},"range":{"tw":[["order",0],["carry",3],["arrange",2],["rate",0],["sight",3],["feed",2],["wide",6],["high",6],["reach",0]],"en":"The shop sells a wide range of goods. The owner likes to arrange them in a strict order: tins at the front, then bread on a high shelf out of a child's reach, and rice at the back. She will carry a box in from the yard herself and set the rate by the morning price. Out of the window a range of low hills fills the sight. She says she came here for that view. Twice a day she has to feed the cat that waits by the door. It is a small place, and she knows every customer by name.","zh":"这家店卖的东西种类很广。店主喜欢把它们按严格的顺序摆好：罐头在前头，面包放到孩子够不着的高架子上，米在后头。她会自己从院子里搬箱子进来，按早上行情定价。窗外一排低低的山占满了视线。她说她来这儿就是为了这片景色。她每天得喂两次守在门口的那只猫。店不大，可每个客人的名字她都叫得出来。"},"reckon":{"tw":[["bet",0],["allow",3],["reason",2],["fret",6],["consider",3],["average",3],["think",2],["surmise",6],["count",0]],"en":"I reckon the trip will take about four hours by train. My brother does not allow for the slow part near the river, so he counts on three. We had a small bet about it, and I let him pick the reason for his number. On average he is right, but I think this time the road will be busy. He began to fret about missing the evening meal. I can only surmise what our aunt will say. We decided to leave at six and consider the whole question again at the station.","zh":"我估计这趟坐火车大概要四个小时。我哥没把河边那段慢路算进去，所以他只按三小时计。我们为这个打了个小赌，我让他说出他那个数目的理由。平均来说他对，可我觉得这回路上会堵。他开始为赶不上晚饭发愁。我只能猜姑姑会怎么说。我们决定六点出发，到车站再把这事重新想一遍。"},"recover":{"tw":[["find",0],["access",3],["better",2],["survive",6],["regain",0],["rally",3],["cover",2],["save",6],["retrieve",0]],"en":"It took my grandfather a long year to recover after the fall. At first he could not find the strength to cross the room, and he needed help to get access to the stairs. Then, slowly, he began to better his own record each week. He had to survive a bad winter, but he would rally in spring. To regain the use of his hand he squeezed a soft ball. He would cover his knees with a warm cloth and smile at us. Old photos helped him retrieve the names of people he had forgotten. The doctor said the rest had helped save his heart.","zh":"爷爷摔了一跤之后，整整一年才恢复过来。起初他连走完一间屋子的力气都找不到，上楼梯还得有人扶。后来他慢慢做到每周都比上一周好一点。他熬过了一个难捱的冬天，可一到春天又振作起来。为了重新用上那只手，他捏一个软球。他会用暖布盖住膝盖，冲我们笑。医生说，好好休息帮他把心脏保住了。老照片也帮他重新想起了许多已经忘掉的名字。"},"register":{"tw":[["read",0],["book",3],["play",2],["entry",6],["record",2],["list",3],["affect",2],["notice",6],["file",0]],"en":"At the front desk I had to register for the summer course. The woman read my name, then wrote it in a long book. She asked me to play it back to her, and I repeated every entry. My record showed that I had paid in spring, so she put a mark on the list and let me choose a room. A small notice on the wall said the office would close at five. Rain could affect the road, she said, and I should keep my file with me. I signed the form and left.","zh":"在前台，我得为暑期课程登记。那位女士看了我的名字，写进一本厚厚的册子。她让我把它复述一遍，我就把每一条都念了出来。记录显示我春天已经交过费，于是她在名单上做了个记号，让我挑房间。墙上贴着一张通知，说办公室五点关门。她说下雨可能影响路况，让我把材料随身带着。我签了表就走了。"},"release":{"tw":[["free",0],["blow",3],["pass",2],["video",6],["issue",2],["pop",3],["flow",2],["date",6],["button",0]],"en":"The band planned to release a new video on Friday. Their last song was a pop hit, and the date was already on every poster. In the first shot a man presses a button, and a door opens to set a bird free. Air seems to flow through the room, and a soft wind makes the curtain blow. A guard lets a visitor pass, then hands him a paper like a release form. The whole thing ends with one long note. The band said they would issue it on paper as well. I watched it twice and could not stop humming.","zh":"乐队打算周五发布一个新视频。他们上一首歌很火，日期早就印在每张海报上了。第一个镜头里，一个男人按下按钮，一扇门打开，放走了一只鸟。空气好像在屋里流动，一阵轻风把窗帘吹起。门卫放一个访客过去，又递给他一张纸，像张放行单。整段最后落在一个长音上。乐队说还会把它印成纸质的。我看了两遍，一直哼个不停。"},"remove":{"tw":[["hit",0],["clear",3],["kill",2],["discard",6],["murder",0],["draw",3],["distance",2],["allow",6],["transfer",2]],"en":"The police came to remove a broken door and clear the yard. A man had been found near the road, and the papers called it a murder, though nobody could explain the hit on his head. Officers used a rope to draw a line in the dust at a short distance from the gate. They would not allow anyone to transfer the boxes inside. One of them told us to discard the wet cloth and kill the flies. I watched them work and said nothing. By noon the road was open again, and the neighbours went back to their lunch.","zh":"警察来拆掉一扇破门，把院子清了出来。有人在路边被发现，报纸上说那是一起凶杀，可谁也说不清他头上那一击是怎么回事。警察用绳子在离大门不远处的灰土上画了条线。他们不许任何人把里面的箱子搬走。有个人叫我们把湿布扔掉，把苍蝇打死。我看着他们干活，什么也没说。到中午路又通了，邻居们回去接着吃午饭。"},"represent":{"tw":[["act",0],["draw",3],["express",2],["particular",6],["play",0],["form",3],["mean",2],["individual",6],["present",0]],"en":"In art class we had to represent our own street on one sheet of paper. I chose to draw the shop at the corner, because it means more to me than the park. A girl in my class used a particular kind of blue to express the evening light. Our teacher said a picture can present a whole life, not just one individual house. Then the older students put on a short play about a family, and each role had to act out a real feeling. My small drawing took a simple form: a door, a lamp, and a cat.","zh":"美术课上，我们要在一张纸上画出自己那条街。我选了街角的店，因为它对我来说比公园更要紧。班里一个女孩用一种特别的蓝来表现黄昏的光。老师说，一幅画能呈现一整个人生，而不只是某一栋房子的样子。后来高年级同学演了一出关于一家人的短剧，每个角色都得把真实的情绪演出来。我那幅小画很简单：一扇门、一盏灯、一只猫。"},"require":{"tw":[["ask",0],["call",3],["order",2],["allow",6],["need",0],["charge",3],["demand",2],["use",6],["want",0]],"en":"This job will require a lot of patience, the manager said. She did not ask for a paper or a call; she only wanted to see my hands. The work would need steady eyes and a strong back, and the order of every step had to be right. The rule did not allow anyone to smoke inside, and the charge for a broken tool came out of our pay. Customers might demand a small change of plan at any moment. I had to use what was in front of me. It was hard, but I said yes.","zh":"经理说，这份活儿需要很多耐心。她没要什么证明，也没让我打电话，只想看看我的手。这活需要眼稳背壮，每一步的顺序都得对。规定不许在里面抽烟，弄坏工具的钱要从工资里扣。客人随时可能要求改个小小的安排。我只能用手边有什么就用什么。这活儿不轻松，可我还是答应了。"},"maximum":{"tw":[["maximise",4],["utmost",0],["limit",2],["minimum",1],["threshold",6],["maximal",0],["zero",6]],"en":"The old pump had a maximum of forty turns, and the men were told to keep it below that limit. Anything above the threshold would damage the seal. To maximise the flow they had to work the handle at a steady pace, never all the way to the top. My uncle did his utmost to keep the needle at zero while I counted. The minimum for the day was twelve turns, and the maximal reading was thirty-eight. He said that was close enough. The needle shook, but it never crossed the red line. We wrote both numbers in the log and went home.","zh":"那台老水泵最多转四十圈，师傅们被告知要把它控制在限度以内。只要超过那个临界值，密封圈就会坏。想把流量开到最大，他们得匀速摇手柄，绝不能摇到顶。我叔叔尽了最大努力让指针停在零位，我在旁边数着。那天最少十二圈，最大读数三十八圈。他说这就差不多了。指针晃了几下，可始终没越过那道红线。我们把两个数都记进了本子，然后回家。"},"peace":{"tw":[["pacify",4],["repose",0],["order",2],["war",1],["progress",6],["treaty",2],["accord",6]],"en":"My grandfather was born in a village that had seen a long war, and he spoke of peace as something you had to build, not simply wait for. He would say that the treaty signed in the town hall brought order back to the fields, and that the two sides had reached an accord at last. He worked to pacify angry neighbours and to keep the small progress they had made. In the evening he liked an hour of repose under the old tree. I never heard him raise his voice. That quiet, I think, was his whole idea of peace.","zh":"我爷爷出生在一个经历过漫长战争的村子里，他谈和平，总说那是要一点点建起来的东西，不是光等着就能来的。他说镇上大厅里签下的和约让田里重新有了秩序，两边总算达成了和解。他常常去安抚发火的邻居，守住他们那点小小的进展。傍晚的时候，他喜欢在老树底下歇上一个钟头。我从没听他抬高过嗓门。我想，那份安静就是他对和平的全部理解。"},"lack":{"tw":[["miss",0],["absence",3],["need",2],["spite",6],["want",3],["deficit",3],["quality",6],["deficiency",0]],"en":"That summer the farm felt the lack of rain more than anything else. The absence of water in the ditch worried my uncle, and in spite of his careful work the young plants began to fail. There was a real deficit in the harvest by August, and the need for help grew each week. He would not want anyone to see how tired he was. The quality of the soil was still good, he insisted. It was a small deficiency, he said, and the next year would be better. I still miss those long evenings in the field with him.","zh":"那年夏天，农场最缺的就是雨。沟里没水，让叔叔很发愁；尽管他干得很仔细，苗还是开始撑不住了。到八月，收成实实在在地亏了，需要人手的地方一周比一周多。他不愿意让人看出自己有多累。他一口咬定，土壤的底子还在，这不过是点小不足，明年会好的。到今天，我还想念跟他在地里度过的那些傍晚。"},"length":{"tw":[["distance",0],["gauge",3],["section",2],["height",6],["duration",0],["altitude",3],["extent",2],["span",6]],"en":"The engineer had to know the length of the new road before anything else, so we walked the whole distance with a tape and a gauge. One section ran along the hill, and there the height and the altitude changed with every step. Nobody could guess the extent of the work until we had the figures. The duration of the job, he said, would depend on the winter. At the far end a short bridge would span the stream, no more than ten steps across. We wrote everything in the book that night. He said we had measured it the hard way, and the right way.","zh":"工程师首先得知道这条新路有多长，于是我们拿着卷尺和量规把整段距离走了一遍。有一段沿着山脚，那儿的坡高和海拔每一步都在变。在看数字之前，谁也估不出这活儿有多大。他说工期长短要看今年冬天的情形。尽头处要架一座短桥跨过小溪，不过十来步宽。那天晚上我们把所有东西都记进了本子。他说，这遍我们是笨办法量的，也是对的量法。"},"locate":{"tw":[["settle",0],["base",3],["find",2],["retrieve",6],["site",0],["map",3],["station",2],["identify",6]],"en":"We had to locate a good place to camp before the light went, and the map on the seat was our only help. My father would study the site of every old station along the line, and then identify the one with water nearby. He wanted to settle on a spot early, so that we could base ourselves there for two nights. When we lost the torch, we had to go back and retrieve it from the grass. In the end we found a flat field by the stream. It was not on the map at all. That turned out to be the best night of the trip.","zh":"天亮之前我们得找到一块能扎营的地方，座位上的那张地图是唯一的帮手。我爸会研究沿线每一个老车站的位置，再找出附近有水的那一个。他想早些定下来，好在那儿待两晚。手电丢了，我们又折回去，从草里把它捡回来。最后我们在溪边找到一片平地。地图上根本没有标。那一晚成了整趟行程里最好的一夜。"},"lump":{"tw":[["ball",0],["clot",3],["symptom",2],["deposit",6],["chunk",0],["bloat",3],["sum",6],["clump",0]],"en":"The doctor felt a small lump under his arm and asked how long it had been there. He said the first symptom had been a dull weight, like a ball of dough, and that the arm had begun to bloat after a week. There was a clot near the surface, and a chalky deposit he could not name. My father had a chunk of ice at home that he used on it every night. The doctor did not seem worried. He wrote down a small sum for the tests and told him to come back in June. Outside, a clump of weeds grew by the door.","zh":"医生在他腋下摸到一个小肿块，问长了多久了。他说最早的症状是那儿发沉，像一团面团，一周后胳膊就开始肿。靠近皮下有一处血块，还有一片说不清是什么的白色沉积。我爸家里常备一块冰，每天晚上敷在上面。医生看起来并不担心。他写下做检查要花的一小笔钱，让他六月再来。门外长着一丛杂草。"},"mail":{"tw":[["post",0],["express",3],["message",2],["telephone",6],["send",2],["register",3],["transfer",2],["page",6]],"en":"My grandmother still goes to the post office to send her letters by mail, though she has a telephone at home. She will not use the express service; ordinary post is enough. Last week she had to register a small parcel and transfer some money for my cousin's school. Then she wrote a short message on a page from her notebook and asked the clerk to read it back. He did, slowly, and she thanked him twice. On the way out she said the old counter felt more honest than any machine. She has done it that way for fifty years.","zh":"我奶奶寄信到现在还是去邮局，尽管家里就有电话。她不肯用快递，普通邮寄就够了。上星期她得寄一个挂号小包，还给我表弟的学校转了一笔钱。然后她在笔记本上撕下的一页写了句短信，让柜员念给她听。他念了，念得慢，她谢了他两遍。出门的时候她说，这老柜台比任何机器都让人踏实。这套做法她用了五十年。"},"maintain":{"tw":[["hold",0],["carry",3],["insist",2],["ensure",6],["assert",0],["allege",3],["conserve",3],["secure",6]],"en":"The old man had to maintain three wooden bridges, and he did it alone. He would hold every board up to the light before he used it, and carry the heavy ones himself. He would insist that a bridge tells you when it is tired, and he would assert that the water was the only real enemy. Some people would allege that he was slow, but nobody could secure a better job. In winter he worked to conserve the timber with oil. He wanted to ensure that nothing he built would fail under a cart. Not one of those bridges has ever fallen.","zh":"那位老人要维护三座木桥，全靠他一个人。用板子之前，他都要举起来对着光看，重的那几块也自己扛。他一口咬定，桥累了自己会告诉你；他还断言，水才是唯一的真敌人。有人说他慢，可谁也没本事换上一份更好的活。冬天他给木料上油保养。他要确保自己造的东西不会在车轮底下垮掉。那三座桥，一座也没塌过。"},"map":{"tw":[["represent",2],["chart",3],["picture",2],["exact",6],["function",0],["expansion",3],["plan",2],["document",6]],"en":"The students had to draw a map of the town as it might look in twenty years. Their teacher asked them to represent every street honestly, and to chart the new houses on the western side. One picture showed a wide road where the market stood now, and the plan for the expansion of the station filled a whole page. The function of each building had to be named in a small box. They had to be exact about the river, since it floods. Their map became an official document, and it still hangs in the hall. Some of the streets they drew are real now.","zh":"学生们要画一张地图，画出这座镇子二十年后的样子。老师让他们如实画出每条街，并把西边的新房子标上去。有一张画把现在集市所在的地方画成了一条大路；车站扩建那部分计划占满了整页。每栋楼的用途都得写在一个小方框里。那条河得过水，所以位置一定要准。他们这张图后来成了一份正式文件，至今还挂在礼堂里。他们画的有些街，现在真的存在了。"},"measure":{"tw":[["bar",0],["clock",3],["carry",2],["limit",6],["beat",0],["last",3],["effect",6],["bill",0]],"en":"The workshop had its own way to measure time: a tall clock by the door and a small bar of steel on the bench. My uncle would carry the same piece of wood from one end of the room to the other and beat it gently on the table, to hear if it rang true. He said that a good tool had a limit, and that going past it had an effect you could not undo. He would last a whole morning on one job. At the end of the month the bill went out with every figure checked twice.","zh":"这间作坊有自己量时间的办法：门边一座高钟，工作台上一小条钢。我叔叔会把同一块木头从屋子这头搬到那头，再轻轻在桌上敲一敲，听它响得正不正。他说好工具是有极限的，越过去，造成的影响就收不回来了。一件活他能干一上午。月底账单寄出去之前，每个数字都核过两遍。"},"monkey":{"tw":[["fiddle",0],["puddle",3],["child",2],["cat",6],["tinker",0],["work",2],["mouse",6],["tamper",0]],"en":"At the small zoo a monkey sat by a puddle and began to fiddle with a piece of wire, turning it over and over in its hands. A child at the fence tried to copy it, and the cat from the farm next door watched from the wall. The keeper said the animal liked to tinker with anything it could reach, and that no lock was safe from it. It would work at the same knot for an hour. Later I found a mouse in the shed at home, and I had to check that nothing had tampered with the seed bags.","zh":"在小动物园里，一只猴子坐在水洼边，开始摆弄一截铁丝，在手里翻来覆去。栅栏边一个孩子想学它，隔壁农场的猫趴在墙上看。饲养员说，这只动物够得着的东西都要拆一拆，什么锁都挡不住它。同一个结它能弄上一个钟头。后来我在家里的棚子里发现一只老鼠，只好仔细查了一遍，看有没有谁动过那些种子袋。"},"mud":{"tw":[["clay",0],["slop",3],["dirty",2],["sand",6],["muck",0],["soil",2],["brush",6],["mire",0]],"en":"After the rain the yard was all mud, and my boots sank into the slop with every step. My aunt makes pots, and she kept a sack of clay and a heap of sand by the door, away from the muck. She said the best soil came from the low field, though it was almost a mire that week. I had to brush the dirty water off the path before anyone slipped. She worked the wet clay with her hands and did not mind the mess. The pots dried slowly on the shelf. By Friday the path was hard and the yard was clean.","zh":"雨后的院子全是泥，每走一步靴子都陷进烂泥里。我姑姑做陶器，门口放着一袋陶土和一堆沙子，离那摊脏泥远远的。她说最好的土出在低地里，虽然那一周那儿几乎成了泥沼。我怕有人滑倒，得先把小路上那层脏水刷掉。她用手揉着湿陶土，也不嫌乱。那些罐子在架子上慢慢阴干。到星期五，小路变硬了，院子也干净了。"},"murder":{"tw":[["hit",3],["slaughter",3],["kill",2],["guilty",6],["remove",0],["homicide",2],["mangle",0]],"en":"The writer was working on a story about a murder in a quiet town. In her notebook the guilty man was never the one the police first hit on, and the homicide squad had to remove three wrong names before the truth came out. She did not like to kill anyone in the first chapter. One draft described how a machine had mangled a coat to hide the proof, and how a farmer at the slaughter house had seen a stranger that night. It was not a cruel book, she said, only a careful one. In her books nobody stays dead for long.","zh":"这位作家正在写一个故事，讲一座安静小镇上的一桩谋杀案。在她本子里，有罪的那个人从来不是警察最先盯上的那个，凶杀组得划掉三个错名字，真相才露出来。她不喜欢在第一章就让人死掉。有一稿写一台机器把一件外套绞烂，好藏住证据；还有个在屠宰场干活的人，那晚看见过陌生人。她说这不是一本残忍的书，只是一本写得仔细的书。在她的书里，没有人能死太久。"},"narrow":{"tw":[["minute",0],["change",2],["wide",1],["edge",6],["contract",0],["strait",2],["broad",6],["constrict",0]],"en":"The fishing boat had to pass through a narrow strait before the tide turned, and the channel was so tight that there was only a minute gap on either side. My father would not let the engine change its note; he wanted it steady. The water was wide and calm outside, but here the rocks seemed to constrict the whole sea. He kept the boat close to the edge of the shore, where he knew every stone. When the tide ran out, the opening seemed to contract, and we had less room still. A broad stretch of open water lay beyond, and we reached it safely.","zh":"渔船得在潮水转向之前穿过一道狭窄的海峡，水道太窄，两边只剩一丁点空隙。我爸不让发动机变调，他要它稳稳的。外头的水面又宽又静，可在这儿，礁石像是把整片海都勒紧了。他贴着岸边走，那一带的石头他都认得。潮水退下去的时候，那道口子像是收紧了，余地更小。过了这儿就是一大片开阔的水面，我们平安地到了那边。"},"occasion":{"tw":[["function",0],["meal",3],["cause",2],["welcome",6],["juncture",0],["party",3],["reason",2],["farewell",6]],"en":"It was a special occasion: my aunt's last week at the factory after thirty years. The whole family came to the farewell meal, and it turned into a small party in the back garden. There was no real cause for sadness, and she made us welcome as always. Her brother gave a short speech, which he had never done at any other function, and even the neighbours came over. At that juncture nobody wanted to talk about work. I asked her the reason she had stayed so long, and she said it was the people. We cleared the table at midnight.","zh":"这是个特别的场合：我姑姑在厂里干了三十年，这是最后一周。全家都来吃这顿告别饭，后来在后面的园子里变成了一个小聚会。其实没什么可难过的，她还是像往常一样张罗着招呼我们。她哥哥讲了几句话——在别的聚会上他从没讲过；连邻居都过来了。到了那个当口，谁也不想再谈工作。我问她，为什么能一待这么多年，她说是因为这些人。到半夜我们才把桌子收拾干净。"},"path":{"tw":[["course",2],["beat",3],["line",2],["parallel",6],["track",3],["walk",3],["direction",6],["route",0]],"en":"There was a narrow path up the hill that my grandfather knew by heart. He would walk it twice a week, and his boots had beaten a line into the grass that ran parallel to the old wall. The route was not marked, but he never lost his course. When the weather turned, he would change direction and take the lower track instead, where the trees kept the wind off. He said a path like that was a friend you could count on. I followed him for years and still do not know the whole course of it. Some mornings he walked it before the sun was up.","zh":"上山有一条窄窄的小路，爷爷闭着眼都认得。他一周走两回，靴子在草里踩出一道线，跟那道老墙平行。路上没有标记，可他从不走错。天一变，他就改个方向，走下面那条车道，那儿的树能挡风。他说这样的路像个靠得住的朋友。我跟着他走了好些年，到现在还没摸清它整条路线的走向。有些早上，太阳还没出来他就走完了。"},"pile":{"tw":[["deal",0],["flood",3],["hair",2],["heap",6],["lot",0],["shock",3],["trash",6],["mess",0]],"en":"We spent a whole Saturday clearing the attic, and what a pile of things we found. There was a heap of old letters, a deal of broken tools, and a lot of boxes nobody had opened since the war. My mother pulled down a shock of grey hair from a hat box and laughed. A flood of dust came with every bag, and we had to carry the trash down in three trips. The room was a real mess by noon. By evening it was empty, and we sat on the floor. We kept two boxes and threw the rest away.","zh":"我们花了整整一个星期六清阁楼，翻出来的东西堆成一座小山。有一摞旧信、不少坏了的工具，还有好多从那时候起就没打开过的箱子。妈妈从一个帽盒里拽出一把灰白的头发，笑了起来。每扔一袋就扬起一片灰，我们分三趟才把垃圾搬下去。到中午屋里乱得不成样子。到傍晚就空了，我们坐在地板上。我们留下了两个箱子，其余的都扔了。"},"pine":{"tw":[["ache",0],["die",3],["wood",2],["oak",6],["yearn",0],["conifer",2],["spruce",6],["yen",0]],"en":"The smell of pine filled the little workshop, and my uncle said no other wood worked so easily under the plane. He had a yen for the old forests, and he would walk among the conifer trees for hours. There was an oak by the gate that had begun to die, and it made him ache to look at it. He would yearn for the days when whole hillsides of spruce stood there. Now he kept a single board of pine on the wall and would not sell it. He said a good tree deserves to be remembered. I still have a small box he made from it.","zh":"松木的气味充满了小作坊，我叔叔说没有别的木头在刨子底下这么顺。他对老林子有股念想，能在针叶树里走上几个钟头。门口那棵橡树开始枯了，看着让他心疼。他总怀念满山云杉还立着的那些年。如今他在墙上留着一块松木板，不肯卖。他说，一棵好树值得被人记住。他用它做的小盒子，我还留着。"},"pity":{"tw":[["shame",0],["care",3],["sympathy",2],["sorry",6],["grieve",2],["utter",6],["compassionate",0],["compassion",0]],"en":"When the old woman next door lost her husband, it was a pity that so few people came to the house. My mother would not just say she was sorry; she would go in and sit with her for an hour. It was no shame to cry, she said, and it was better to grieve openly than to keep it all in. Her sympathy never sounded like a speech. She did not utter one careless word, and she never asked for anything back. She had real compassion, and she tried to be compassionate with everyone, even those who had never cared about the old woman.","zh":"隔壁老太太失去丈夫的时候，来她家的人那么少，真让人心里不是滋味。我妈不只是说一句节哀，她会进屋陪她坐上一个钟头。她说，哭出来不丢人，放声地悲伤总比全憋在心里强。她的同情从不像是背出来的话。她一句轻率的话都没说，也从不图什么回报。她心里真有怜悯，也尽量对每个人都体贴，连那些从来没关心过老太太的人也一样。"},"plug":{"tw":[["secure",0],["tap",3],["advertise",2],["fix",6],["chew",0],["close",2],["brake",6],["punch",0]],"en":"The old pump would not start, so my father had to pull the plug, tap the pipe with a small hammer, and fix the leak before anything else. He told me never to chew on a wire or punch the switch when I was tired. He would secure every joint with a second turn of the tool. There was a small card by the bench that seemed to advertise a brand of oil, but he never used it. When the motor ran again, he would close the lid and press the brake on the wheel to keep the machine still. It worked for another year.","zh":"那台老泵不转了，我爸只好先拔下插头，用小锤敲了敲管子，把漏处修好再说别的。他告诉我，累了的时候千万别咬着电线干活，也别乱拍开关。每个接头他都要再把工具转上一圈，拧得牢靠。工作台边有张小卡片，好像是给一种机油做广告的，他从来没用过。马达重新转起来以后，他会把盖子合上，再踩住轮子上的刹车，让机器稳住不动。它又撑了一年。"},"protest":{"tw":[["resist",0],["strike",3],["complain",2],["rally",6],["dissent",0],["demonstrate",3],["oppose",2],["riot",6]],"en":"Last spring the drivers on the small bus route began to complain about their pay, and in the end they voted for a strike. The people on our street held a quiet protest at the depot, not because they wanted to oppose the drivers, but because they had no other way to get to work. One speaker said she would resist any plan to cut the route altogether, and a few neighbours chose to dissent from the louder voices. There was a rally on the green, where the children carried signs and a woman began to demonstrate how to fold them. It never turned into a riot. By June the buses were running again.","zh":"去年春天，那条小公交线上的司机开始为工资抱怨，最后投票决定罢工。我们街上的人在车场外安静地抗议，倒不是要跟司机们对着干，而是因为没有别的办法去上班。有位发言人说，谁要干脆取消这条线，她一定顶回去；也有几个邻居选择不跟着嗓门最大的那些人走。草坪上开了个集会，孩子们举着牌子，一位女士还教大家怎么折这些牌子。事情始终没有变成骚乱。到六月，公交车又跑起来了。"},"regard":{"tw":[["consider",3],["identify",3],["look",2],["contrary",6],["see",0],["stare",2],["respect",6],["view",0]],"en":"My grandmother kept one photograph that she would look at every evening. She said she had great regard for the woman in it, though I could not identify her at first. On the contrary, I had always taken her for a stranger. When I asked, she told me to consider how the light fell and to stare at the hands rather than the face. From that view the likeness was clear, and I began to see my own mother in it. Her respect for the old picture never faded. She would not let anyone move it. It hangs where she can see it from her chair.","zh":"奶奶留着一张照片，每天晚上都要看上一眼。她说照片上那个女人她很敬重，可我一开始认不出那是谁。恰恰相反，我一直当她是个陌生人。我问起来，她让我注意光是怎么落下来的，别盯着脸，去看那双手。从那个角度看，相像之处一下子就清楚了，我也在里面看见了我妈。她对这张旧照片的敬重从没有淡过。谁也别想挪动它。它就挂在她坐在椅子上能看见的地方。"},"relief":{"tw":[["rest",0],["breath",3],["comfort",2],["save",6],["ease",0],["reprieve",3],["help",6],["respite",0]],"en":"When the doctor finally came out and said the operation had gone well, my mother let out a long breath. It was such a relief that she had to sit down. The news gave us a short respite from three weeks of worry, and for one evening we had real comfort in that cold corridor. The nurse said the worst was behind us and we should go home and rest. There was no easy way to repay the help we had been given. It felt like a reprieve, and even the small tea from the machine seemed to ease everything. The doctors had caught the trouble in time to save her sight.","zh":"医生终于出来说手术很成功，我妈长长地舒了一口气。她一下子松下来，只好坐下。这个消息让三周的担心暂时停了一停，那个晚上，我们在冰冷的走廊里得到了真正的安慰。护士说最坏的已经过去，让我们回家歇着。人家给的帮助，我们怎么谢都不算多。那种感觉像得了宽限，连机器里那杯小茶都好像把一切都抚平了。医生们发现得及时，保住了她的视力。"},"remark":{"tw":[["mention",3],["knock",3],["state",2],["speech",6],["note",2],["courtesy",3],["rebuke",6],["notice",2]],"en":"At the meeting my father made one short remark about the fence, and then said no more. He did not mention any names, and he was careful to state only what he had seen. The chairman wrote a note and thanked him for his courtesy. Later, someone gave a long speech that turned into a quiet rebuke of the whole committee. There came a knock on the table, and the room went silent. I did not notice that my father had left until the meeting ended. He never liked to be the one who spoke last. I found him waiting for me by the gate.","zh":"会上我爸就那道篱笆简短说了一句，之后再没开口。他没有点任何人的名字，只小心地说出自己看到的事。主席记了笔记，谢他这么有礼。后来有人讲了一大段话，实际上是对整个委员会的一场委婉责备。桌子被敲了一下，屋里静了。我一直到散会才发现我爸早走了。他从来不喜欢当最后说话的那个人。我出门时看见他在门口等我。"},"reserve":{"tw":[["allow",0],["preserve",3],["military",2],["cap",6],["book",0],["request",2],["current",6],["hold",0]],"en":"The valley had been made a nature reserve, and the rules were strict. Visitors were not allowed to camp, and there was a cap on the number of cars each day, so you had to book a place and send a written request. A small military post stood at the far end, left from another time. The current in the river was strong, and there were places where you could not even hold a line. The rangers worked to preserve the old trees and to keep the water clean. I walked there all morning and saw no one. It is one of the last quiet places I know.","zh":"这条山谷被划成了自然保护区，规矩很严。游客不许露营，每天进来的车也有限额，得先订位置，再寄一份书面申请。最里面有个小小的军事哨所，是早年间留下的。河里的水流很急，有些地方连钓线都撑不住。巡护员们忙着保护那些老树，也守着水质的干净。我在那儿走了一上午，一个人也没碰见。这是我知道的少数几处还安静的地方之一。"},"loan":{"tw":[["lend",0],["trust",3],["word",2],["credit",6],["advance",3],["debt",2],["mortgage",6]],"en":"The bank would not give my parents another loan, so a neighbour offered to lend them the money himself. He asked for nothing on paper, only their word that it would come back. My father had never taken an advance from anyone before, and the debt sat on him like a stone. He paid back every month, even when the mortgage took most of his pay. In the end it was a matter of trust, not credit. Years later he still spoke of that man with respect. He never once missed a payment, not in three years.","zh":"银行不肯再给我爸妈贷款了，于是邻居主动提出借钱给他们。他不要任何字据，只要他们一句会还的承诺。我爸从没向谁预支过钱，那笔债压在他身上像块石头。他每个月都还，哪怕房贷已经占去大半工资。到头来这是一份信任，不是信用的事。多年以后他提起那个人，语气里还是敬重。三年里，他从没漏过一期。"},"male":{"tw":[["virile",0],["man",3],["animal",2],["female",1],["adult",6],["chap",3],["young",6]],"en":"On the farm the male of the pair was easy to tell from the female, because only he had the long tail. A grown animal like that can look strong and virile, but this one was gentle. The young ones followed the female all day, while the male sat on the fence and watched. An old chap who worked there told me the male would stay near the nest for weeks. He was a quiet man and said little. An adult bird like that, he said, is a better parent than most people think.","zh":"农场里，这一对里哪只是雄的很好认，因为只有它有长尾巴。像那样长大的动物看着又壮又有雄性气概，可这一只很温和。小的们整天跟着雌鸟，雄鸟却停在篱笆上看着。在那儿干活的一个老头告诉我，雄鸟会在巢边守好几个星期。他话不多。他说，这样一只成年鸟，多数人想象不到它有多会照顾孩子。"},"march":{"tw":[["edge",0],["file",3],["touch",2],["process",0],["troop",3],["walk",2],["border",0]],"en":"At dawn the troop began its long march along the border road. They moved in single file, close to the edge of the field, and nobody spoke. The process was slow, and every man had to touch the shoulder of the one in front when the mist grew thick. I watched them walk past the old wall for an hour. At the end of the line a young soldier turned and looked back at me. Then they were gone, and the road was empty again. I stood by the gate until the last sound had died away.","zh":"天一亮，那支队伍就沿着边境公路开始长途行军。他们排成一列纵队，紧挨着田边，谁都不说话。整个过程很慢，雾一浓，每个人就得摸前面那人的肩膀。我看着他们从老墙边走过，看了一个钟头。队伍末尾一个年轻士兵回过头看了我一眼。然后他们就走了，路上又空了。我在门口站着，直到最后一点声响都消失。"},"memory":{"tw":[["store",0],["recall",3],["faculty",2],["physical",6],["retention",0],["hardware",2],["computer",6]],"en":"My grandfather's memory began to fail the year he turned eighty. He could recall a whole song from his youth but not what he had eaten that morning. The doctor said memory is not one faculty but many, and that his physical health mattered as much as his age. I bought him a small computer and tried to store every family photo on it. His retention of new things stayed poor, though he learned to press one button. The hardware sat on his desk, mostly unused, but he liked having it there.","zh":"爷爷八十岁那年，记性开始不行了。他能想起年轻时候的一整首歌，却记不住早上吃了什么。医生说记忆不是单独一种能力，而是好几种，他的身体状况和年纪一样要紧。我给他买了台小电脑，想把家里的照片都存进去。他对新东西记不住，不过还是学会了按一个键。那台机器多数时候摆在桌上没人动，可他很喜欢它在那儿。"},"minister":{"tw":[["pastor",0],["work",2],["prime",6],["rector",0],["attend",2],["cabinet",6],["parson",0]],"en":"The minister of our small church had served there for forty years. He would work all week and then attend to anyone who came to the door, whether they needed a pastor or simply a listener. He was not a rector with a big house, just a quiet parson who kept his notes in an old cabinet. The prime lesson he gave us was to sit with people in silence. I met him once as a child, and I can still see his hands. He never raised his voice, not even when the roof leaked and the rain came in.","zh":"我们小教堂的牧师在那里服侍了四十年。他平时干活，到了门口有人来就去照应，不管人家要的是牧师还只是一个愿意听他说话的人。他不是住大宅子的教区长，就是个安静的牧师，把笔记收在一个旧柜子里。他教给我们最重要的东西，是安静地陪着别人坐一会儿。我小时候见过他一面，到现在还记得他的手。他从不大声说话，哪怕屋顶漏雨、雨水灌进来也一样。"},"mood":{"tw":[["climate",0],["sulk",3],["tone",6],["temper",0],["peeve",3],["attitude",6],["modality",0]],"en":"After the operation my uncle was in a poor mood for weeks. The climate of the whole house changed with him: if he sulked at breakfast, nobody laughed at dinner. My aunt learned to read his tone before she said a word about the weather. His temper had always been short, and the smallest thing could peeve him. The doctor said a different treatment modality might help, and that a calm attitude would matter more than any pill. Slowly he came back to himself. He even began to joke about the food, which was never good.","zh":"手术之后，我叔叔好几个星期心情都不好。整栋房子的气氛也跟着他变：他早饭时生闷气，晚饭时谁都不敢笑。我婶学会了先听他的语气，再开口谈天气。他脾气一向急，最小的事也能把他惹恼。医生说换一种治疗方式也许有用，还说平和的心态比什么药都重要。他慢慢恢复了过来。他甚至开始拿伙食开玩笑，那儿的饭从来不好吃。"},"motor":{"tw":[["drive",0],["engine",3],["machine",2],["automobile",6],["motive",0],["travel",2],["car",6]],"en":"The old motor in my grandfather's car had not started for two winters. My father would drive out on Sundays, open the engine, and stand there for an hour. He said every machine has a motive of its own, and this one simply wanted attention. He cleaned it, oiled it, and talked to it as if it could hear. On the first warm day it turned over and ran. The whole automobile shook, then settled into a steady sound, and we travelled down the lane and back. It was the last time that car ever moved.","zh":"爷爷那辆车上的旧马达已经两个冬天没发动过了。我爸每个星期天都会开车出去，打开引擎，站在那儿一小时。他说每台机器都有自己的脾气，这一台不过是想要人搭理。他把它擦干净、上油，还跟它说话，好像它听得见。第一个暖和的日子，它终于转起来、着了火。整辆车抖了一阵，然后稳下来，我们沿着小路开出去又开回来。那是那辆车最后一次动起来。"},"nest":{"tw":[["cuddle",0],["gather",2],["pond",6],["nestle",0],["gang",2],["brood",6],["snuggle",0]],"en":"By the pond a pair of birds had built a nest low in the reeds, and the whole brood was always hungry. The young ones would nestle together and cuddle in the cold, while the mother gathered food from the water. A gang of older birds sometimes came near, and she would fly at them until they left. In the evening the family would snuggle down and go quiet. I watched them for a long time from the far bank. Nobody in the house believed me when I told them how close it was.","zh":"池塘边有一对鸟在芦苇里低处筑了个巢，一窝雏鸟总也吃不饱。天冷时小家伙们挤在一起互相依偎，母鸟则从水里找吃的。有时一群大鸟凑过来，她就冲过去把它们赶走。傍晚一家子偎下来，渐渐安静了。我在对岸看了很久。回家跟他们说离得那么近，谁都不信。"},"opposite":{"tw":[["opponent",0],["word",2],["alternate",1],["along",6],["reverse",0],["close",6],["contrary",0]],"en":"In the debate my opponent sat opposite me, and we had almost nothing in common. He would say one word, and I would say its reverse, as if we were reading from two different books. We took alternate turns for an hour along a long table, and the room grew quiet. Afterwards a teacher told us that contrary views often sit close together. I did not agree at the time. Now I think it was the truest thing said that day. We shook hands at the end, which surprised the whole room, and I have thought about that hour ever since.","zh":"辩论时我的对手就坐在我对面，我们几乎没有一点相同。他说一个词，我就说它相反的那个，好像两人读的是两本不同的书。我们沿着一张长桌轮流发言一个小时，屋里越来越静。后来一位老师说，相反的观点常常离得很近。当时我不服。现在我觉得，那是那天说得最对的一句话。结束时我们握了手，满屋子人都吃了一惊，那一个钟头我到现在还常想起。"},"partner":{"tw":[["mate",0],["husband",3],["act",2],["firm",6],["consort",3],["associate",2],["foster",6]],"en":"My partner and I had run the small firm for eleven years. He was also my husband, which made the quiet weeks easier and the hard ones worse. We had to act as one in front of the staff, even when we disagreed at night. His old associate still came in twice a week, and my mate from school did our books. Some people thought we were a strange consort, a married pair who worked side by side. But we tried to foster one idea above all: that nobody should be afraid to speak.","zh":"我和合伙人一起经营这家小公司十一年了。他还是我丈夫，这让平淡的日子好过些，难熬的日子更难过。在员工面前我们得步调一致，哪怕晚上在家吵过。他以前的同事每周还来两趟，我上学时的好友帮我们做账。有人觉得我们这对搭档奇怪——两口子天天并排干活。但我们一直想培育一个念头：谁都不该怕开口。"},"pause":{"tw":[["break",0],["freeze",3],["interrupt",2],["wait",6],["hesitate",0],["rest",3],["hurry",6]],"en":"There was a long pause before my brother answered the phone. I could hear him breathe, and for a moment I thought he would freeze and say nothing. I did not want to interrupt him, so I waited. He had always been in a hurry, never able to rest for a minute. This time he seemed to hesitate over every word. Then he said he would take a short break from work and come home. I put the phone down and sat still, and the pause in the room felt like something solid. It was the first time in years that he had asked me for anything.","zh":"弟弟接电话前停了很久。我能听见他的呼吸，有一会儿我以为他会僵在那儿，什么也不说。我不想打断他，就等着。他一向急性子，一分钟都歇不下来。这回他好像每个字都要犹豫一下。然后他说，他要从工作里歇一小段，回家来。我放下电话，坐着没动，屋里那阵停顿像是有实体的东西。这是他这么多年来第一次开口向我要什么。"},"pen":{"tw":[["write",0],["draw",3],["swan",2],["pencil",6],["compose",0],["creep",3],["paper",6]],"en":"That winter I learned to draw with a pen, because my father said a pencil was too easy to rub out. I would sit by the window and try to write my name in one steady line. On the paper a swan was the hardest thing of all, and mine always looked like a badly shaped boat. Then he would compose a few simple shapes for me, and I would copy them until my hand stopped shaking. In the evening the cold would creep into the room, and we would put the work away. The lines I made that winter were never good, but I kept them all.","zh":"那年冬天我学着用钢笔画画，因为我爸说铅笔太容易擦掉。我会坐在窗边，试着一笔不停地写下自己的名字。纸上最难画的就是天鹅，我画出来的总像一条难看的船。于是他给我拼出几个简单的形状，我就照着描，直到手不再抖。到了傍晚，冷气一点点钻进屋里，我们就把东西收起来。那个冬天我画出的线条一直不算好，可我全都留着。"},"period":{"tw":[["stop",0],["watch",3],["end",2],["early",6],["flow",0],["discharge",2],["since",6]],"en":"For a long period after the accident I could not watch a car go past without closing my eyes. The worst of it came early, in the first weeks, when I could not stop thinking about the sound. Then the flow of days began to slow, and the fear thinned out. Since that spring I have slept better. At the end of my stay the hospital gave me a paper of discharge, and I walked out into the sun. That period of my life is over, though I still turn away from fast roads. My brother says I will forget it one day.","zh":"出事之后很长一段时期，我看不得有车经过，一看见就闭眼。最难的时候来得很早，头几个星期，那声音在我脑子里停不下来。后来日子一天天流过去，慢了下来，害怕也淡了。从那年春天起我睡得好多了。住院结束的时候，医院给了我一张出院单，我走到太阳底下。那段日子过去了，只是现在看见快车道我还是会别过脸。我弟弟说，总有一天我会把它忘掉。"},"pig":{"tw":[["cop",0],["live",2],["cow",6],["fuzz",0],["swine",2],["rabbit",6],["hog",0]],"en":"One of our pigs got out of the pen and went straight through the vegetable garden. My father called it a swine under his breath and ran after it with a bucket. The hog was faster than it looked, and it lived near the fence for two days before we caught it. A cop from the village came by to ask if we had lost anything, which made us laugh. There was soft fuzz on its back, and it liked the carrots best. Even the cow and the rabbit in the next field seemed to watch the whole chase.","zh":"我们的一头猪拱出了猪圈，直接穿过菜园。我爸低声骂了句蠢猪，拎着桶就追。那家伙跑起来比看上去快，在篱笆边住了两天我们才逮住它。村里一个警察顺路过来问我们有没有丢东西，把我们都逗笑了。它背上有软软的绒毛，最爱吃胡萝卜。连隔壁地里的牛和兔子好像都在看这场追逐。"},"pocket":{"tw":[["bag",0],["space",2],["wallet",6],["steal",2],["boot",6],["scoop",0],["sack",0]],"en":"In my coat pocket there was a small space where I always kept my keys, and that morning the wallet was gone. I checked the bag, the sack by the door, and even my boot. Someone had taken it in the market, in the few seconds I turned to pay. I felt a hot scoop of shame rather than anger. I told myself it was only money, but my hands would not stay still. I never found out who had dared to steal it, and for months I kept my hand over that pocket in any crowd.","zh":"我大衣口袋里有一小块地方，平时总放着钥匙，那天早上钱包不见了。我翻了包、门口的麻袋，连靴子都看了。在市场上，就我转身付钱那几秒钟，有人把它拿走了。我心里涌上来的是一勺滚烫的羞愧，而不是愤怒。我告诉自己那不过是钱，可手就是停不下来。偷的人我始终没找到，后来好几个月，一到人多的地方我就把手按在那个口袋上。"},"polish":{"tw":[["finish",0],["glaze",3],["better",2],["round",0],["slick",3],["perfect",2],["culture",0]],"en":"Every Saturday my uncle would polish the old table until it was slick to the touch. He had learned the work in a workshop where they would glaze wood and then round each corner by hand. A good finish, he said, was a kind of culture, something you could not hurry. He wanted every surface perfect, and each year it grew better than the last. I liked to watch the cloth move in slow circles. When he was done, the table caught the window light, and the whole room seemed cleaner. He would not let anyone else touch it.","zh":"每个星期六，我叔叔都会把那张旧桌子擦得锃亮，摸上去滑手。这手艺是他在一家作坊里学的，那里的人会给木头上釉，再用手把每个角磨圆。他说好的收尾功夫本身就是一种教养，急不来。他要求每一处都完美，而一年一年它确实比上一年更好。我喜欢看那块布慢慢地转圈。等他做完，桌面映着窗光，整个屋子都像干净了。他不让别人碰那张桌子。"},"pray":{"tw":[["beg",0],["crave",3],["plead",2],["bless",6],["implore",0],["commune",2],["wish",6]],"en":"In the last week of her illness my grandmother asked us to pray with her each evening. She did not beg for more time, and she never once implored the sky to spare her. She would plead only that the family stay close after she was gone. We would commune in the small room while the light went down. She said she did not crave anything more, and that she wished us well. When we finished, she would bless each of us by name, one after another. I still say those words sometimes, alone, when the house is quiet.","zh":"她病重的最后一周，奶奶让我们每天晚上陪她祈祷。她没有乞求更多时间，也从不哀告上天放过她。她只恳求一件事：她走以后，一家人要亲近。天一点点暗下去，我们就在那间小屋里与她灵交。她说她再没有什么渴求，只愿我们安好。念完之后，她会一个一个叫我们的名字，为我们祝福。有时我一个人待着，屋里静下来，还会念那些话。"},"prevent":{"tw":[["forbid",0],["stop",3],["avoid",6],["preclude",0],["defend",3],["protect",6],["foreclose",0]],"en":"The village built a low stone wall to prevent the river from taking the road again. For years nobody could stop the water when it rose, and no one could forbid people from building too near the bank. We met to avoid the same mistake twice, and to protect the three houses at the end. The new wall would preclude any easy path for the flood, though nothing could foreclose the chance of a very bad year. My father helped lay the stones. He said we were not defending property; we were defending the people who lived there.","zh":"村里修了一道矮石墙，免得河水再冲走那条路。多年来，水一涨谁也没法拦住，也没人能禁止大家在离岸那么近的地方盖房。我们聚在一起商量，为的是不再犯同样的错，也为了保住路尽头那三户人家。新墙会堵住洪水最容易走的那条路，不过谁也没法排除碰上极坏年份的可能。我爸帮着垒石头。他说我们护的不是财产，是住在那儿的人。"},"purple":{"tw":[["royal",0],["lavender",3],["pink",6],["imperial",0],["mauve",3],["yellow",6],["regal",0]],"en":"In the late summer the hills behind the house turned purple with lavender, and the air smelled of it for weeks. My mother would cut a few stems and put them in a jar on the table. She said the colour looked royal, almost imperial, though the flowers were small and plain. Beside them she set a yellow bowl, and the two colours made the room feel warmer. A mauve cloth hung on the wall, and next to it a pink one. She had a way of making a plain house look regal with almost nothing.","zh":"到了夏末，屋后的山坡被薰衣草染成一片紫，空气里好几个星期都是那股味道。我妈会剪几枝插在桌上的罐子里。她说这颜色看着高贵，简直像皇家的，可花本身又小又朴素。她还在旁边放了一只黄碗，两种颜色让屋子显得暖了些。墙上挂着一块淡紫色布，旁边是一块粉的。她总有办法，用几乎什么都没有的东西，把一间普通的屋子弄得很有气派。"},"rat":{"tw":[["shop",0],["inform",2],["snake",6],["bum",0],["work",2],["cat",6],["crumb",0]],"en":"A rat had been living behind the shelves in our shop for a week, and every morning I found a fresh crumb trail near the flour. My mother said we should inform the owner before it came into the front room. We tried a trap, but the animal was quick as a snake and always slipped away. An old bum who slept by the door told us a cat would work better than any poison. So we borrowed one. The rat was gone in two nights, and the cat stayed, sleeping in the window as if it had always belonged there.","zh":"有一只老鼠在我们店的货架后面住了一个星期，每天早上我都能在面粉旁边发现新的碎屑痕迹。我妈说，得趁它跑到前屋之前通知店主。我们试过夹子，可那家伙快得像蛇，每次都溜掉。睡在门口的一个流浪汉说，养只猫比什么药都管用。于是我们借了一只。两天夜里老鼠就没了，猫留了下来，睡在窗台上，好像它一直就属于那儿。"},"relax":{"tw":[["loose",0],["act",2],["tense",1],["dictate",6],["slack",0],["change",2],["hurry",6]],"en":"My shoulders stayed tense for days after the meeting, and nothing I did seemed to help me relax. My sister told me to let my hands go loose and stop letting work dictate every hour of my life. I tried to act as if I had all the time in the world, which was harder than it sounds. There was a slow change over the next week. I began to sleep better and to walk without that tight hurry in my step. On Sunday I sat in the garden doing nothing at all, and the slack afternoon felt like a gift.","zh":"开完那个会以后我的肩膀紧了好几天，做什么都松不下来。我姐叫我让手放松，别让工作支配我生命里的每一个钟头。我试着装出一副时间多得用不完的样子，这比听起来难。接下来一个星期里，变化慢慢来了。我睡得好了，走路时那种紧赶慢赶也没了。星期天我坐在花园里什么也不做，那个松散的下午像是一份礼物。"},"replace":{"tw":[["exchange",0],["reduce",3],["change",2],["substitute",3],["shift",3],["regenerate",2],["interchange",0]],"en":"The old machine in the workshop had to be replaced, and the manager asked us to find a substitute before the end of the month. The plan was to exchange two small units for one large one, which would reduce the noise a lot. It meant a shift in how we worked, and a change none of us liked at first. Someone had to regenerate the part list and set up an interchange with the other team. I spent a week reading manuals. In the end the new machine was quieter, but I still missed the old one.","zh":"作坊里那台旧机器得换了，经理要我们在月底前找到替代的东西。方案是用两台小的换一台大的，这样噪音能小很多。这意味着工作方式的转变，也是我们一开始都不喜欢的一种改变。还得有人重新整理零件清单，跟另一个小组做个交换安排。我读了整整一星期说明书。最后新机器是安静些，可我还是想念旧的那台。"}}});
